            "description": "## Problem to solve\n\nFinish the approved release-one clarification: Pig Boss naming, project-scoped streams, multiple projects in one AWS installation and basic manager health.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n* Reconcile the product, architecture, scenarios and complete Story set; preserve the owner review before implementation.\n* Obtain independent design and delivery-plan reviews with explicit coverage and all seven principles.\n* Publish the final Jira descriptions, dependencies, estimates and acceptance cases; keep all delivery automations inactive.\n\n## Technical Acceptance Criteria\n\n* Design and grooming only. This Task adds no runtime implementation or live AWS/Jira configuration. Fifty-project scaling is a separate follow-on.\n* Repository for design/evidence: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard. Follow current customer-owned architecture, not archived platform plans.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n* Human product/technical reviewers walk each stated outcome and failure boundary against the final design and evidence.\n* Record examined scope, unresolved decisions, evidence limits and independent review verdicts.\n* No delivery runs or production writes are authorized by this planning item.\n\n",
