            "description": "Owner approved the same-scope PGB-78 split on 15 November 2026. R1-24 is the prepared QA publisher; PGB-78/R1-08 retains integrated dispatch and original acceptance. No activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\n# Problem to solve\nproblem_to_solve: An authorized QA caller has no separate skill for delivering a complete prepared\n  assessment to Jira. Evidence and pending human tests need a verified handoff even when execution\n  cannot finish.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-74\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-76\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-77\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-108\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n# Acceptance Criteria\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: An authorized caller can use qa-jira directly to check a configured native Story/Bug in\n      QA and publish its complete prepared assessment for the current assignment, review and open\n      PR; other native types are rejected before writes.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Complete passing AI evidence or explicit human-only work moves to Human Review only\n      after verified publication; human cases remain pending.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: A confirmed in-scope defect or known upstream request queues rework; inability blocks;\n      discussion stays QA without a terminal record.\n  - id: AC4\n    requirement: Full partial results, findings and pending human IDs survive failure; unknown writes\n      stop without replay, replacement records or competing transitions.\n  - id: AC5\n    requirement: Installed guidance explains direct invocation, prerequisites, evidence ownership,\n      success and recovery, and makes clear that prescribed dispatch remains a separate pending\n      Story.\n# Technical Acceptance Criteria\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own the qa-jira read-only eligibility and canonical publication/transition skill,\n      its installation, tests and guides, and the approved same-scope 24-Story delivery mapping;\n      execute no tests or manager actions.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer code changes\n      - Archived runtime reuse\n      - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n    - id: D03\n      decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n      reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n    - id: D04\n      decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label; equal\n        labels in different projects are independent. One customer installation supports multiple\n        projects. Basic manager health is in release one; worker monitoring and scaling\n        implementation remain follow-ons.\n      reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: qa-jira is the sole permanent publication/failure contract; use existing canonical\n        records, validators, formatter and direct configured edges, with no new engine, schema,\n        provider adapter or helper transition authority.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Verify current configured scope, actors, assignment/review/PR/requirements receipts and\n        complete evidence before publication; append once, verify exact readback and freshness,\n        transition once and verify status; retain full partial results and never replay completed\n        mutations.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Human-only static work needs no invented deployment; successful runtime completion or\n        any PASS/FAIL claim requires current trusted environment proof, while a complete all-NOT_RUN\n        non-completing report may describe missing deployment under the corrected shared contract.\n# Testing Strategy\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed\n      customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Prescribed isolated fixture set for all cases below; each case states its input and\n        expected outcome. All unmentioned snapshot facts are complete/valid and no earlier-priority\n        work exists.\n      initial_state: Fresh per case; only explicitly sequenced actions share state. Providers/tool\n        receipts are simulated, credentials dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Executable local fixtures and exact commands for all human cases below, bound to the PR\n        revision.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-24-H01\n        - R1-24-H02\n        - R1-24-H03\n      preserves:\n        - All case inputs, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup. No live provider data or\n          changed test expectations.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which the currently\n      approved automated QA skills do not execute. Human reviewers run these cases; developer CI and\n      PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-24-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC5\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n        prerequisites:\n          - Prepared native Story and Bug assessments with a complete mixed API-child/database/UI\n            ledger, declared observed-value binding, inspectable supplied/mock screenshots, exact\n            human IDs and current valid receipt chains.\n          - Same-release installed qa-jira and private disposable fixtures with simulated provider\n            cards and dummy credentials.\n        steps:\n          - Follow the installed direct-invocation guide and call preflight, then final, for each\n            native type.\n          - Inspect the full ledger, evidence retrieval, human_pending and ordered tool audit.\n          - Check predecessor validation, append, exact comment readback/chain, freshness, direct\n            transition and independent native-status verification.\n          - Inspect the approved 24-Story mapping, new R1-24 before unchanged R1-08, preserved\n            downstream dependencies and current-versus-historical review statements.\n        expected:\n          - Every prescribed nested row and pending human ID is retained; only verified\n            current-revision completion reaches Human Review.\n          - The caller can use the publisher without a dispatcher; the guide states dispatch remains\n            pending and installation grants no authority or activation.\n          - The delivery records retain all existing R1 IDs, 53 product requirements and 41\n            scenarios; the original three R1-08 human cases remain, and R1-24 adds three publication\n            cases without claiming acceptance.\n        evidence:\n          - Input/output hashes, exact installed path/revision/command, ordered tool audit,\n            inspected screenshots, typed ledger, receipt chain and delivery-mapping diff.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-24-H02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n        prerequisites:\n          - Separate coherent prepared defect, known-upstream-wait, inability,\n            earlier-FAIL-plus-later-inability, earlier-FAIL-plus-wait and discussion assessments;\n            upstream requests include their exact typed lineage.\n        steps:\n          - Call final on each fresh assessment without running helpers.\n          - Inspect final/partial ledger, findings, unfinished NOT_RUN reasons, exact upstream\n            references and publication/transition audit.\n        expected:\n          - Confirmed defect and known outstanding wait select Rework Queued; inability selects\n            Blocked while retaining earlier findings and evidence; discussion has no terminal write\n            and stays QA.\n          - A rumor cannot become a dependency request, omissions or unresolved finding IDs reject,\n            and human cases never become PASS.\n        evidence:\n          - Exact prepared and produced records, full receipt chain, selected destination,\n            verified/unknown status, tested revision and exact command.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-24-H03\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Static human-only native Bug with empty AI graph/types, two pending human IDs and a\n            nonempty no-AI reason.\n          - Separate Task/Epic, changed source/requirements/stage, missing/stale deployment,\n            untrusted approval, missing receipt page, oversized ledger, definite append failure,\n            unknown append/readback, unknown transition and explicitly authorized resume variants\n            with a known completed mutation.\n        steps:\n          - Call preflight/final for the zero-AI Bug, then each separate invalid or failure variant.\n          - For missing deployment, compare a complete all-NOT_RUN blocker with a report claiming\n            PASS/FAIL.\n          - Inspect call audit, retained evidence, receipt resolution, current/unknown status and\n            any resume action.\n        expected:\n          - Valid static work invokes no helper or environment request, keeps the exact pending\n            human list and reaches Human Review only after verified publication.\n          - Invalid native types stop before writes; complete all-NOT_RUN inability may publish a\n            valid blocker, while execution claims without required proof reject.\n          - Stale/unknown effects stop without mutation replay, fallback terminal writes or\n            overwriting a changed stage; at most one resolving read follows each uncertain action,\n            and only conclusive success permits the next distinct step.\n          - Resume consumes existing explicit valid human authorization and retained case-specific\n            evidence; it never creates authorization, repeats a completed mutation or auto-passes\n            humans.\n        evidence:\n          - Input/output hashes, ordered tool audit, human handoff, retained evidence/receipt reads,\n            tested revision and exact command.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live\n              records/resources.\n  automated_regression: Canonical accepted/rejected publication records, full partial ledgers,\n    human-only handoff, uncertain-write handling and source/installed skill-validator-formatter\n    parity; no prose-only claim of runtime behavior.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
