            "description": "Director authorized the independently reviewed same-scope PGB-81 split on 15 November 2026. R1-25 delivers the existing repeated-parent chain validator; PGB-81/R1-11 retains the complete preview and all 42 original cases. Provisional — not ready for delivery until corrected PGB-80 merge, final-base binding and two independent concrete-plan reviews. Source publication is pending the first validator PR. No activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: The existing local chain validator rejects a legitimate repaired child that\n  consumes older and newer updates from its actual parent. Workers and operators cannot validate the\n  complete repair even when every required cause is present.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-80\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: The existing source and installed chain command validates current B2\n      implementation/review/QA consuming exact U1+U2 at verified A3, retaining R1 and R2 without\n      duplicate leaf consumption.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Historical U1/A2 remains valid nested evidence; selecting stale U1/A2 as current still\n      fails its current-pointer/stage/PR checks.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Divergent parent history, missing causes, invalid immutable metadata, duplicate direct\n      requests and cycles reject without changing supplied data or authorizing execution.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own existing canonical receipt repeated-parent validation, source/installed tests\n      and guides, plus the approved same-scope delivery-record amendment for this validator and\n      PGB-81; no related repository changes.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer code changes\n      - Archived runtime reuse\n      - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n    - id: D03\n      decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n      reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n    - id: D04\n      decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label; equal\n        labels in different projects are independent. One customer installation supports multiple\n        projects. Basic manager health is in release one; worker monitoring and scaling\n        implementation remain follow-ons.\n      reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Preserve public chain inputs/results and strict current completion,\n        role/metadata/PR/no-publication/resume rules with zero provider effects; add no public\n        permissive option, manager history export or preview policy.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Prove same-parent successors through actual repair-admission previous_assignment\n        ancestry with preserved parent/PR/project/full-stream/repository identity; retain each\n        direct request once and exact effective repair roots without weakening inherited QA\n        execution proof.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Reuse the exact immutable 28-record chronology and complete current-phase synthetic\n        envelopes; change only selected target and B outer stage, retain source/variant hashes and\n        never derive expected outcomes from production validation.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout, actual same-release installed chain command and\n      prepared disposable local synthetic fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Frozen 28-record repeated-parent H02 chronology, nine checkpoints and separate\n        phase-bound C01 controls with fixed independent expectations; C02/C03 use fresh copies.\n      initial_state: No live provider data or credentials; frozen originals and all 119 prepared files\n        remain unchanged; only disposable variants are edited.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Executable local fixtures and exact source/installed commands bound to the PR revision;\n        separately hash and diff all C01 phase variants, retain completed-stage negatives and\n        isolate the repeated-parent RED failure on the final corrected PGB-80 base.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-25-C01\n        - R1-25-C02\n        - R1-25-C03\n      preserves:\n        - All original receipt bytes, references/digests, authors/times, complete pages, retained\n          metadata, requirements, pointers, PR facts and request resolutions.\n        - Fixed C01 validity/completion and C02/C03 rejection outcomes; no invented receipt, edited\n          oracle, credentials or provider effects.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which the currently\n      approved automated QA skills do not execute. Human reviewers run these cases; developer CI and\n      PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-25-C01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Prepared DATA-01, source checkout and actual same-release installed validate-handoff\n            command; dummy data only, no credentials, network or deployed target.\n          - Frozen checkpoints/08-b2-full-qa/receipts/b2_qa.json with all 28 immutable records,\n            complete 14/10/4-comment pages and all 28 retained