at proven A3; common R1 is\n            covered once, R2 remains covered and no cause is dropped.\n          - Only QA81028 establishes completion; phase-valid implementation81026 and review81027 do\n            not.\n          - The unchanged completed checkpoint rejects implementation/review selected as current at\n            /target/stage_id; its QA target remains valid.\n          - Inputs and frozen history remain byte-identical; no provider/state writes or execution\n            authorization occur; synthetic observations do not claim earlier real chronology.\n        evidence:\n          - Exact source and installed commands, selected target, tested commit,\n            exit/result/diagnostics, zero-write audit and source/variant SHA256 before and after\n            execution.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain commands, output, tested revision and before/after input hashes; remove only\n              disposable variants and installed test output, never the frozen chronology or live\n              records.\n      - id: R1-25-C02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - C01 phase-bound controls, immutable A2/U1 references and later current outer\n            observations from DATA-01; each control starts from a fresh copy.\n          - No receipt is resealed and no source body, digest, metadata, pointer, current PR or\n            native observation is changed to make a stale target pass.\n        steps:\n          - Select authentic old A2 completion and U1 stack publication separately as current\n            targets under their unchanged later observations.\n          - Run each through source and actual installed chain commands in readable and JSON modes;\n            retain exact 