            "description": "This same-scope preparation prerequisite supports PGB-78. It preserves the original PGB-78 outcome and cases. Full dispatch remains pending PGB-78; no activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: The prescribed PGB-78 QA cases need complete inputs that the existing helpers and\n  publisher can consume without reconstructing missing facts. Current helper preparation needs\n  manual completion, while publisher preparation starts with finished assessments.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-74\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-76\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-77\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-108\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-110\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-138\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A developer or human QA reviewer can prepare the declared mixed Story and Bug inputs,\n      inspect every artifact and invoke the existing helpers with their exact declared inputs before\n      PGB-78 is implemented.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Preparation preserves requirements, case order, child ownership, declared bindings,\n      human cases and negative controls; it supplies no observed result, completed ledger or chosen\n      destination.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Incomplete identity, artifact, extraction, operation or timing facts remain visible\n      before execution; existing static, partial and retained-evidence inputs keep their correct\n      proof boundaries.\n  - id: AC4\n    requirement: The existing producer and reviewer guidance explains how to prepare and inspect these\n      inputs, retain actual helper evidence and pass an independently formed assessment to qa-jira,\n      while full dispatch remains pending PGB-78.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Complete PGB-78 PREP-01 mechanical input preparation in the existing source-only QA\n      fixture module, its tests and producer/consumer guidance; keep existing helper, raw-work,\n      prepared_inputs and qa-jira contracts.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer code changes\n      - Archived runtime reuse\n      - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n    - id: D03\n      decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n      reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n    - id: D04\n      decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label; equal\n        labels in different projects are independent. One customer installation supports multiple\n        projects. Basic manager health is in release one; worker monitoring and scaling\n        implementation remain follow-ons.\n      reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Reuse the existing same-release parsers, receipt validators, fixture exporters and\n        installed helper/publisher interfaces without adding a schema, runtime dispatcher, QA engine\n        or provider adapter.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Keep supplied/mock input facts separate from actual observed outputs and private\n        expectations; preserve existing publication fixtures and leave the new output directory\n        empty.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Bind raw work, trusted context, artifact hashes, actor, tenant, allowed actions and\n        current PR/environment proof independently; no missing proof may be replaced by an expected\n        value or ticket assertion.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed\n      customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Fixed supplied/mock inputs for the three preparation acceptance cases; independent\n        variants use fresh private folders.\n      initial_state: Fresh per case; only explicitly sequenced actions share state. Providers/tool\n        receipts are simulated, credentials dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Executable source-only preparation and exact commands for R1-27-H01 through R1-27-H03,\n        bound to the reviewed PR revision and existing helper/publisher interfaces.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-27-H01\n        - R1-27-H02\n        - R1-27-H03\n      preserves:\n        - All case inputs, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup. No live provider data or\n          changed test expectations.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which the currently\n      approved automated QA skills do not execute. Human reviewers run these cases; developer CI and\n      PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-27-H01\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC4\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Prepared same-release checkout and installed helper/publisher roots; fixed native Story\n            and Bug mixed API-child, PostgreSQL and UI inputs; dummy access and explicitly\n            supplied/mock provider facts.\n        steps:\n          - Prepare a fresh private input folder with the exact command supplied by PREP-01 and\n            record source, installed and input hashes.\n          - Inspect raw work/context, declared preparation consumers, selected request/assertions,\n            query/parameter layout, UI route/checkpoints, extraction mapping and separate\n            access/deployment facts.\n          - Invoke each existing helper through its declared caller with actual earlier outputs;\n            preserve returned parent/child results, query facts and screenshots.\n          - Form an assessment from those actual results and invoke qa-jira with the fixed\n            supplied/mock read/write cards; inspect readback and transition evidence.\n        expected:\n          - Every required input is present and retains its declared type and consumer; an output is\n            bound only after its real helper observation.\n          - The preparer produces no assessment or verdict; existing helpers and publisher can\n            consume the handoff without a new dispatcher or reconstructed fact.\n          - Mock evidence stays labelled mock; human cases remain pending and no live mutation\n            occurs.\n        evidence:\n          - Exact commands, source/installed/input hashes, preparation artifacts, original helper\n            results, screenshots, independently formed assessment and ordered simulated tool audit.\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain inputs, actual output and evidence first; remove only the owned disposable\n              preparation folder without changing live records or resources.\n      - id: R1-27-H02\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Fresh positive controls and independent missing extraction, query, UI checkpoint,\n            identity/tenant, operation-bound and explicit dependency-cause variants; finite\n            observation inputs for both completion policies.\n        steps:\n          - Inspect each positive input with the same delivered contract and validator.\n          - Inspect each named negative in a fresh folder and attempt only its existing read-only\n            preflight or input validation.\n          - Compare unchanged expected outcomes and case/step IDs with the original controls;\n            inspect that no expected result or completed output was substituted.\n        expected:\n          - Positive preparation identifies every fact needed by the existing consumer.\n          - Each negative stays incomplete or is rejected at the matching existing boundary; none\n            becomes ready through a guessed value, inferred permission or rewritten requirement.\n          - Finite observation offsets and whole-unit bounds are supplied as inputs; the preparer\n            executes no schedule or mutation.\n        evidence:\n          - Raw original and negative inputs, parser diagnostics, completeness observations, exact\n            missing-field/cause references and empty generated output directories.\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain inputs, actual output and evidence first; remove only the owned disposable\n              preparation folder without changing live records or resources.\n      - id: R1-27-H03\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Static human-only Bug, all-NOT_RUN missing-environment partial, earlier FAIL then\n            inability, pure upstream wait, retained FAIL plus wait, and valid/invalid\n            retained-evidence input controls from the existing publisher families.\n        steps:\n          - Prepare each independent control and inspect raw requirements and predecessor versus\n            current-result separation.\n          - Inspect the static pending-human list and the exact proof required by each partial or\n            reused claim.\n          - Follow the documented existing helper/publisher input handoff and recovery guidance;\n            compare the original publication suite before and after preparation.\n        expected:\n          - Static human-only work requires no invented environment; any supplied PASS/FAIL or\n            reused claim retains its actual nonnull tested PR and trusted current-revision\n            environment proof.\n          - Pure wait and retained-FAIL wait remain distinct and carry a current-case cause; later\n            inability preserves earlier findings.\n          - Original publication inputs remain unchanged, new execution outputs remain empty, and\n            neither preparation nor documentation claims human acceptance or activation.\n        evidence:\n          - Commands and hashes, original versus emitted input comparison, proof/cause observations,\n            exact pending humans, recovery notes and original publication-fixture preservation\n            check.\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain inputs, actual output and evidence first; remove only the owned disposable\n              preparation folder without changing live records or resources.\n  automated_regression: Use the existing raw work and receipt validators plus independent artifact\n    checks to verify complete helper/publisher input preparation, consumer bindings, preserved\n    negative inputs and empty execution outputs.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
