            "description": "Provisional — not ready for delivery. R1-34 in the Pig Boss release-one set. Preparation draft only; no activation is authorized. Actual reviewed/merged PGB-145 rebind and Director publication gates remain.\n\n```yaml\n# Provisional — not ready for delivery. No Jira publication or implementation is authorized by this draft.\n# Native title: Inspect complete scoped Jira inventory\n# Source identity: reserved R1-34; native parent Epic PGB-66. Native key is not allocated here.\n# Reviewed plan SHA256: 858c3e8d02a8ae0b3cd810f1e2e00a70dedcd3515cfe18f415a98ef0828f3cb4\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\n\n# Problem to solve\nproblem_to_solve: Named-issue inspection cannot find occupied work omitted from a caller's list. A\n  manager caller needs the union of opt-in work, native membership, retained work and typed\n  references, with honest limits and ownership changes.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-147\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A source/copied library call returns complete or explicitly incomplete native inventory\n      for the configured domain, with retained-source completeness reported separately.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Discovery covers all-status opt-in seeds, native children and exact full-label\n      occupancy, then fresh-reads the union of declared, retained, prerequisite and typed-reference\n      identities to a bounded fixed point.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Missing/drifting/denied reads and exhausted limits retain known observations and\n      old/current ownership; failures identify a proven isolated scope or shared uncertainty.\n  - id: AC4\n    requirement: Immutable project/issue IDs preserve equal-label separation, renamed keys and\n      cross-project references; collecting a prerequisite never marks it satisfied.\n  - id: AC5\n    requirement: The documented source/copied harness demonstrates complete, failure and\n      unrelated-history cases without writes, receipt acceptance, state mutation or admission\n      claims.\n\n# Technical Acceptance Criteria\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own complete scoped native inventory and reference collection using B1’s reader,\n      with source/copied harness, distribution, tests, documentation and publication metadata.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer repository changes, AWS resolver/wrapper, State adapter and\n        operational-state writes.\n      - Receipt acceptance, policy selection/admission, external PR/evidence fetching, a new input\n        producer or a PGB-144 proof-policy decision.\n      - Production live CLI, provider probes, deployment, activation, worker monitoring, Cursor\n        deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines.\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions: []\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Repository `danielchappell/Pigboard`, base `main`, one PR; own scoped inventory and\n        reference acquisition using B1's fixed reader, with complete docs/distribution/publication\n        tests.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Use the same single canonical config and invocation accounting. The supplied object has\n        exactly retained_members, pending_intents and explicit retained_complete. Retained members\n        carry ticket_id, project_id, epic_id, label and assignment (null or\n        ticket_id/comment_id/record_id/digest); pending intents carry project_id, label, ticket_id\n        and attempt_id. Validate existing bounded field shapes, unique records and configured\n        site/project bindings. Missing or false retained completeness never becomes empty complete\n        state or new setup authority.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Search only fixed enhanced-JQL families; follow actual search tokens and comment\n        offsets separately, preserve former ownership and never crawl unrelated project history.\n    - id: TAC4\n      requirement: Existing work/handoff parsers identify candidate references only; completeness does not\n        establish visibility, current receipt proof, trusted context, capacity or policy success.\n\n# Testing Strategy\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout, actual prepared copied runtime and disposable local\n      HTTPS fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Prescribed isolated B2 fixture set for the four human groups below, including only\n        their listed finite variants and controls.\n      initial_state: Fresh per variant; only explicitly paired controls share their stated sequence.\n        Provider responses are scripted and credentials are dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: PR-bound executable local HTTPS fixture scripts, literal reports and permitted request\n        traces, exact source/copied commands and prepared absolute paths for every listed variant;\n        all expected answers are authored independently of the production collector.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-34-H01\n        - R1-34-H02\n        - R1-34-H03\n        - R1-34-H04\n      preserves:\n        - All acceptance criteria, technical constraints, case inputs, finite variants and limits,\n          paired controls, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup.\n        - Existing source/copied distinction, verified TLS and no-effects boundaries; no live\n          provider data, changed expectations, new cases or raised budgets.\n        - \"All original PGB-82 acceptance remains on final82: five AC, three TAC and four human\n          groups, including full integrated preview and offline-equivalent policy results.\"\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/library contracts, which the currently approved\n      automated QA skills do not execute. QA skills are []; human reviewers run the prescribed\n      cases. Developer regressions, CI and independent PR review remain required and do not count as\n      human acceptance.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-34-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC5\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the PR-bound local fixture packet DATA-01, exact commands, literal\n            expected reports and maximum permitted call traces before execution; do not generate\n            expected answers from the production collector.\n          - Prepared Node and root validator dependencies, source checkout and actual copied\n            runtime; fresh disposable data per variant, dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS\n            fixture servers. No live Jira account, AWS, Postman or UI is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: complete-domain, unrelated-history,\n            retained-incomplete. Each uses fresh state except its explicitly paired controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - For each listed variant, run the prepared source command using node\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs --case R1-34-H01 --variant NAME --runtime\n            SOURCE_ROOT --json; PREP-01 supplies each exact variant name and absolute prepared root.\n          - Compare the report and permitted request audit with the literal expectations below;\n            inspect actual counters, bytes, elapsed time and cleanup.\n          - Repeat the same variant through the actual copied runtime from an unrelated working\n            directory, using the copied harness and --runtime COPIED_ROOT; PREP-01 supplies the\n            exact copied command and absolute root.\n          - Inspect no-effects and cancellation evidence and compare source/input/server\n            before-and-after hashes. Where the guide-and-install variant prescribes readable output,\n            also run its human form without --json and compare its meaning with JSON.\n        expected:\n          - \"complete-domain: opted-in and paused Epic, undeclared child, Human Review/Blocked\n            occupancy outside the Epic, retained member, declared prerequisite and typed target\n            closure; literal complete ID/provenance set with present pointers. unrelated-history:\n            add exactly 65 unrelated historical issues with 512 total comments to the server script;\n            queries/reads and result stay identical, no unrelated ID/comment access.\n            retained-incomplete: same data with explicit false retained_complete yields shared\n            incomplete.\"\n          - Native completeness and retained completeness remain separate; no result grants\n            admission, prerequisite success or receipt proof.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested PR revision, source/copied runtime identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            source/copied commands.\n          - Command/output transcripts, exit codes, safe reports and literal expected-report\n            comparison.\n          - Permitted request trace, actual request/count/byte/time measurements,\n            no-effects/cancellation observations and before/after hashes.\n          - Cleanup result and any remaining unverified outcome; these local fixture observations do\n            not prove live Jira, AWS, supported production capacity or activation.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the evidence packet and close the prescribed local fixture servers, sockets and\n              timers; the resolver-late fixture stops and acknowledges its own I/O where that\n              variant applies.\n            - Remove only disposable fixture/build directories and damaged copies; preserve the\n              usable prepared release, source and retained evidence. Do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-34-H02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n          - TAC4\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the PR-bound local fixture packet DATA-01, exact commands, literal\n            expected reports and maximum permitted call traces before execution; do not generate\n            expected answers from the production collector.\n          - Prepared Node and root validator dependencies, source checkout and actual copied\n            runtime; fresh disposable data per variant, dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS\n            fixture servers. No live Jira account, AWS, Postman or UI is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: seed-page-missing, child-page-missing,\n            label-page-missing, token-repeat, token-missing, search-duplicate,\n            fresh-membership-change, malformed-seed, malformed-record, reference-missing,\n            reference-digest-change, reference-cycle, epic-limit, stream-l