            "description": "R1-36 in the Pig Boss release-one set. This source prerequisite delivers the complete inspection library and importable fixture API; PGB-147 retains the runnable fixture CLI and installed-runtime completion. The split plan passed two independent reviews. Publication does not mean implementation, acceptance or activation.\n\n```yaml\n# Native title: Inspect named Jira issues from source\n# Source identity: R1-36; native key assigned only by actual create/readback.\n# Reviewed split plan SHA256: 5f94612e3ae7d77210daba67361cef2ef3e8cb3fcf662156d74d825b648c1e47\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: An authorized source caller cannot obtain bounded native issue and comment\n  observations through Pigboard’s supported library. It needs useful partial results and safe\n  failure information without running a manager or installing a copied delivery bundle.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-145\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-152\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-154\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-155\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-156\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A caller can inspect named immutable issue IDs, assignment pointers, all comment pages\n      and supplied exact comment targets through the source library.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Partial, denied, changed or bounded reads retain valid observations and explain missing\n      information without claiming absence or completeness.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Invalid inputs invoke no credential resolver, and all actual requests obey the fixed\n      HTTPS destination, TLS checks and finite count/byte/time bounds.\n  - id: AC4\n    requirement: Safe reports exclude secrets and bodies, expose cancellation limits honestly, and never\n      claim whole-domain completeness, receipt proof or admission.\n  - id: AC5\n    requirement: The documented source API and finite source fixture packet work with prepared\n      dependencies, including source-root damage recovery and preservation evidence.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own the complete source lib/jira/read.mjs API, importable fixture API, source\n      verification, documentation and publication support in the reviewed18-path plan; the runnable\n      fixture CLI and installed distribution remain PGB-147.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer repository changes, AWS resolver/wrapper, State adapter and\n        operational-state writes.\n      - Receipt acceptance, policy selection/admission, external PR/evidence fetching, a new input\n        producer or a PGB-144 proof-policy decision.\n      - Production live CLI, provider probes, deployment, activation, worker monitoring, Cursor\n        deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines.\n      - Runnable fixture CLI, human/JSON CLI parity and installed named-issue inspection; PGB-147\n        owns that completion.\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions: []\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Repository danielchappell/Pigboard, base main; own the complete source inspection API,\n        source verification/docs and publication support in one18-path PR.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Preserve inspectJiraIssues(configInput, request, {resolveSecret}) and PGB-145’s\n        canonical configuration; no production transport hook, live CLI, arbitrary URL, extra\n        credential source or environment bypass.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Preserve native IDs/server metadata, endpoint-specific pagination and all literal\n        observation, trace, status, limit, canary, private-data and cancellation assertions in\n        the35-variant packet, eight controls and L06 private subvariant; generic404 or visibility\n        limits never prove absence.\n    - id: TAC4\n      requirement: Keep runnable fixture CLI and installation publication outside this slice; count all\n        attempted requests/bytes, bound private observations, cancel owned I/O, fence late resolver\n        values, hash the complete source/input/server data and close fixture resources without\n        scheduling or receipt proof.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Reviewed Pigboard source checkout with prepared dependencies and disposable local\n      HTTPS fixtures; no installed inspection claim or deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Prescribed source inspection packet for the four source human groups, with the\n        existing35 variants, eight controls and L06 private subvariant.\n      initial_state: Fresh per variant; only explicitly paired controls share their stated sequence.\n        Provider responses are scripted and credentials are dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: PR-bound importable source runFixture API, independently authored literal\n        reports/acquisition and permitted traces, exact executable source API examples and prepared\n        absolute source path for every listed variant; no expected answer comes from the production\n        collector.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-36-H01\n        - R1-36-H02\n        - R1-36-H03\n        - R1-36-H04\n      preserves:\n        - All reviewed source acceptance criteria, technical constraints,35 finite variants, eight\n          controls, L06 private subvariant, inputs, limits, order, expected outcomes, evidence and\n          cleanup.\n        - Verified TLS, fixed transport, secret/canary safety, all budgets and source/input/server\n          preservation; no provider data, new cases, raised bounds or changed literal expectations.\n        - Source inspection is immediately usable through inspectJiraIssues and importable\n          runFixture; the dedicated CLI and installed completion remain PGB-147.\n        - All original PGB-147 fiveAC/fourTAC/fourhuman groups and source/copied obligations remain\n          on147; all original PGB-82 fiveAC/threeTAC/fourhuman groups remain on final82.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns source library and fixture API contracts, which the\n      currently approved automated QA skills do not execute. QA skills are []; designated human\n      reviewers run these cases. Developer regressions, CI and independent PR review remain\n      separate.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-36-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC4\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the reviewed source fixture packet DATA-01, executable importable API\n            example, literal expected report/private observations and maximum permitted traces\n            before execution; do not derive answers from the collector.\n          - Prepared Node22.17.0 and lock-matching source dependencies, reviewed source checkout and\n            fresh disposable data per variant; dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS servers.\n            No live Jira, AWS, Postman, UI, installed runtime or dependency fetch/repair is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: complete, empty-comments, renamed-key,\n            unknown-pointer, exact-mismatch. Each uses fresh state except its explicitly paired\n            controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - Import runFixture and fixtureCases from the explicit reviewed source root’s\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs; select the listed variants with stable fixture\n            selector R1-33-H01, then await runFixture(v.case, v.variant, SOURCE_ROOT) for each.\n            PREP-01 supplies the exact module example and absolute root; the source fixture has no\n            direct-entry CLI.\n          - For each selected variant with control, await runFixture(v.case, v.variant, SOURCE_ROOT,\n            {control:true}); for L06 also await runFixture(v.case, v.variant, SOURCE_ROOT,\n            {privateProjection:true}). Use only the existing eight controls and one private\n            subvariant.\n          - Compare the returned safe report, private-acquisition oracle and permitted request audit\n            with the literal expectations; inspect counters, bytes, elapsed time, cleanup and the\n            actual late-delivery acknowledgment where prescribed.\n          - Inspect zero-effects/cancellation and source/input/server before-and-after hashes,\n            record the source revision, exact module invocation and returned structured results,\n            then retain evidence and close/remove only disposable fixture resources.\n        expected:\n          - \"complete: two issues, one present pointer each, two comment pages plus one named exact\n            target, literal IDs/metadata and requested complete/domain false. empty-comments:\n            explicit zero-total page, present pointer. renamed-key: same ID/current key.\n            unknown-pointer: pointer404 yields incomplete/POINTER_UNKNOWN, never null.\n            exact-mismatch: changed exact body/metadata yields CHANGED_INPUT.\"\n          - Every library inspection report has inspection_scope requested_issues, domain_complete\n            false, admission not_evaluated and receipt_proof not_evaluated; requested completeness\n            never certifies the whole domain.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested source PR revision, source/dependency identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            programmatic source invocation; no installed-runtime claim.\n          - Programmatic invocation transcript, process exit code, safe returned report and\n            independently authored literal report/private-acquisition comparison.\n          - Permitted request trace, actual request/count/byte/time measurements,\n            no-effects/cancellation observations and before/after hashes.\n          - Cleanup result and any remaining unverified outcome; these local fixture observations do\n            not prove live Jira, AWS, supported production capacity or activation.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the evidence packet and close the prescribed local fixture servers, sockets and\n              timers; the resolver-late fixture stops and acknowledges its own I/O where that\n              variant applies.\n            - Remove only disposable fixture/build directories and damaged source-derived copies;\n              preserve the reviewed source and retained evidence. Do not change live records or\n              repair/fetch dependencies.\n      - id: R1-36-H02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n          - TAC4\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the reviewed source fixture packet DATA-01, executable importable API\n            example, literal expected report/private observations and maximum permitted traces\n            before execution; do not derive answers from the collector.\n          - Prepared Node22.17.0 and lock-matching source dependencies, reviewed source checkout and\n            fresh disposable data per variant; dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS servers.\n            No live Jira, AWS, Postman, UI, installed runtime or dependency fetch/repair is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: missing-page, changed-total, duplicate-comment,\n            zero-progress, issue403, issue404, rate429, header-timeout, body-timeout,\n            resolver-reject, resolver-abort, resolver-late. Each uses fresh state except its\n            explicitly paired controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - Import runFixture and fixtureCases from the explicit reviewed source root’s\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs; select the listed variants with stable fixture\n            selector R1-33-H02, then await runFixture(v.case, v.variant, SOURCE_ROOT) for each.\n            PREP-01 supplies the exact module example and absolute root; the source fixture has no\n            direct-entry CLI.\n          - For each selected variant with control, await runFixture(v.case, v.variant, SOURCE_ROOT,\n            {control:true}); for L06 also await runFixture(v.case, v.variant, SOURCE_ROOT,\n            {privateProjection:true}). Use only the existing eight controls and one private\n            subvariant.\n          - Compare the returned safe report, private-acquisition oracle and permitted request audit\n            with the literal expectations; inspect counters, bytes, elapsed time, cleanup and the\n            actual late-delivery acknowledgment where prescribed.\n          - Inspect zero-effects/cancellation and source/input/server before-and-after hashes,\n            record the source revision, exact module invocation and returned structured results,\n            then retain evidence and close/remove only disposable fixture resources.\n        expected:\n          - \"missing-page, changed-total, duplicate-comment, zero-progress, issue403, issue404,\n            rate429, header-timeout, body-timeout, resolver-reject, resolver-abort, resolver-late:\n            each has a literal stop point/code; no retry, swallowed secret, false absence or\n            post-return B-owned read. Late resolver case expects cancel_unconfirmed and discards the\n            late dummy token; fixture itself acknowledges/stops its own I/O during cleanup.\"\n          - Every library inspection report has inspection_scope requested_issues, domain_complete\n            false, admission not_evaluated and receipt_proof not_evaluated; requested completeness\n            never certifies the whole domain.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n          - resolver-late delivers its dummy token once after the bounded source call returns,\n            acknowledges settlement under active guards and drains one event-loop checkpoint; zero\n            before/after Jira calls, aborted signal and unchanged at-return cancel_unconfirmed\n            report. No larger deadline or timed sleep.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested source PR revision, source/dependency identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            programmatic source invocation; no installed-runtime claim.\n          - Programmat