            "description": "Director authorized this same-scope delivery allocation on 16 November 2026 after two independent full delivery-plan reviews. Exact-base planning, prerequisites, sizing and normal delivery gates remain required. No activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: Existing native consumers need complete authenticated target facts, and reconciliation also needs real native\n  transition history. The current bounded reader has comments but no native changelog operation.\nprerequisites:\n- ticket: PGB-160\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-147\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-148\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-150\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n- id: AC1\n  requirement: The source and installed native receipt route produce exact recorded proof for the requested target using configured\n    authority and complete native closure.\n- id: AC2\n  requirement: For an original retained attempt, the same bounded session produces complete publication observations and separate\n    native status-change history, including a truthful complete-empty result.\n- id: AC3\n  requirement: Missing, denied, incomplete, unsupported or exhausted observations return precise unavailable/incomplete/unsupported\n    outcomes; acquisition writes no provider or operational state.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Read exact handoffs and reconciliation facts through the existing consumers and exact path forecast in\n      the delivery plan.\n    out_of_scope:\n    - Customer repository changes, activation or deployment\n    - Context service, public phase framework, parallel preview generation or new permission source\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n  - id: D-ROLE\n    decision: Owner10906 assigns Pig Boss complete deterministic scheduling and recorded-proof checks; workers retain current\n      applicable execution proof.\n    reference: https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-144?focusedCommentId=10906\n  - id: D-PREP\n    decision: Director10909 permits in-stage current fact preparation from existing authority; only the implementer fills\n      declared mechanical slots and every action requires its applicable proof.\n    reference: https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-144?focusedCommentId=10909\n  constraints:\n  - id: TAC1\n    requirement: Compose the actual handed-off reader session and planned readReconciliationFacts({attempt,publicationReferences,limits});\n      consume validated retained selectors and preserve original package/configuration/assignment/attempt identity.\n  - id: TAC2\n    requirement: Add only fixed GET /rest/api/3/issue/{id}/changelog with startAt/maxResults and native ID/actor/from/to/time\n      projection, sharing counters/deadline/byte limits with issue/comment/publication reads; no generic GET, response-URL\n      following or fresh-budget reader.\n  - id: TAC3\n    requirement: Preserve HTTPS/TLS, destination and secret boundaries, prior retained metadata and exact manager-target bindings;\n      comments cannot substitute for native history, and history alone proves neither 204/409 outcome nor operation correlation.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n  - id: DATA-01\n    description: Finite isolated fixtures for every control stated in this ticket; all other facts are valid and no earlier-priority\n      work exists.\n    initial_state: Fresh per control unless an ordered sequence is explicit; provider/model/helper outputs are simulated and\n      credentials dummy.\n    reference: null\n    preparation_id: PREP-01\n    owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n  - id: PREP-01\n    owner: implementer\n    supplies: Executable fixtures and exact source/copied commands or instruction invocations for the prescribed cases, bound\n      to the reviewed PR revision.\n    used_by:\n    - DATA-01\n    - PGB-163-H01\n    - PGB-163-H02\n    preserves:\n    - All prescribed inputs, ordering, expectations, evidence and cleanup; no invented authority, capability or live result.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI and instruction contracts that the approved API/database/UI helpers do not\n      execute; designated human reviewers run these cases. Developer regression and contributor QA evidence are separate.\n    cases:\n    - id: PGB-163-H01\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC1\n      - AC2\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Prepared bounded REST fixtures for a current QA target and original manager admission/stack-update targets, with exact\n        comments, retained tuples, publication references and native changelog pages; separate complete-empty history variant.\n      steps:\n      - Run exact native receipt and original-attempt reconciliation acquisition through source and copied consumers.\n      - Inspect exact selectors, shared request/byte/time accounting, proof bindings, native-history projection and mutation\n        audit.\n      expected:\n      - All requested pages/proofs bind to the original target and attempt; actual history ID/actor/from/to/time is separate\n        from typed-record ancestry.\n      - Complete empty history remains complete empty, not transition proof; the producer does not assert 204/409 or finalize\n        an attempt and performs zero mutations.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n    - id: PGB-163-H02\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC3\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Missing page, 403/404, exhausted shared budget, timeout, foreign/redirect destination, secret-bearing error, wrong\n        UUID/assignment, edited metadata, absent prior retained tuple and unsupported changelog-shape controls.\n      steps:\n      - Run each isolated acquisition control under the same configured session limit.\n      - Inspect bounded calls, provenance/status and sanitized diagnostics.\n      expected:\n      - No failure becomes empty complete data or fabricated identity; exact unsupported/incomplete reasons remain visible.\n      - No second budget, arbitrary destination, credential leak, write or automatic replay escapes the configured boundary.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n  automated_regression: Update affected source/copied integration or instruction-contract regressions for these prescribed\n    outcomes, retain strict primitive/security regressions and run required repository checks.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
