                  "body": "Published the reviewed role-delivery allocation under the Director's integration disposition.\n\n* PGB-159: complete scheduling declarations; PGB-160: authenticated recorded handoffs; PGB-161: current worker proof and truthful inability; PGB-162: recorded-proof offline preview; PGB-163: exact native handoffs and reconciliation history.\n* PGB-164, PGB-165 and PGB-166: existing implementer, reviewer, and QA/human-rework caller changes. PGB-167 is the separate five-file documentation Task.\n* PGB-82 retains its identity, parent, To Do status, original five AC/three TAC/four cases, with only the reviewed additions and dependencies on PGB-162/163. PGB-144 remains completed.\n\nAll nine Story contracts (including residual PGB-82) were read back against the reviewed draft after mechanical real-key binding. Sixteen new Blocks links were verified; no private issue aliases or null prerequisite keys remain. Current Epic inventory at this readback is 50 Stories and 7 Tasks (57 children); this is native inventory, not a shipped/source-catalogue count.\n\nBoth independent full delivery-plan reviews are CLEAN for plan SHA256 `98916b2ab8dab5e36fc2f753c97b94e2f0e49fe3f188e8a09dbacdc00f397aa4`, covering all nine contracts, 59 criteria, 22 designated human case groups and 76 distinct planned paths. No acceptance execution is claimed. Product review SHA256 `ccb42f76c8cf0f7bd053986fd64e17496cffcbddad36488e859fba62ccec8370`; technical review SHA256 `13fa2c0a9552f57689a9839cca7eeaf5415749150d21ebd40db7cdb3f7f91d9a`.\n\nPGB-81 finishes naturally. PGB-159 follows its actual completed base and must recheck its tight 20-file/12–15.5h whole-slice forecast before code. The first later Core change owns the complete machine catalogue/guard amendment; PGB-167 contains no such code. The 84.5–117h mapped Core/caller subtotal excludes later host/State/apply/release work and is neither net amendment cost nor total remaining project cost. Later source-dependent sizing remain