            "description": "Owner approved the same-scope split on 15 November 2026. PGB-78/R1-08 retains the complete original integrated QA outcome and original case IDs; PGB-110/R1-24 supplies its publisher. No activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\n# Problem to solve\nproblem_to_solve: QA needs to run the named cases in order and hand the open PR to humans. It must\n  retain incomplete results and keep human tests visibly pending.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-74\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-76\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-77\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-108\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-110\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-132\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n# Acceptance Criteria\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: QA accepts native Story/Bug assignments and rejects other types; Grok High dispatches\n      exactly the prescribed top-level steps in order, including declared helper calls/bindings and\n      bounded read-only observation schedules.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Every AI step has PASS/FAIL with evidence or NOT_RUN with reason/finding; pending human\n      case IDs remain separate.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: All AI cases passing, or explicit human-only zero-AI work, publishes verified QA\n      evidence then moves to Human Review.\n  - id: AC4\n    requirement: Confirmed in-scope defects or known upstream waits queue rework; inability blocks;\n      discussion stays QA. Human cases are never auto-passed.\n# Technical Acceptance Criteria\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own QA orchestration and compose the separately delivered qa-jira publisher;\n      helpers retain no transition authority.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer code changes\n      - Archived runtime reuse\n      - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n    - id: D03\n      decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n      reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n    - id: D04\n      decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label; equal\n        labels in different projects are independent. One customer installation supports multiple\n        projects. Basic manager health is in release one; worker monitoring and scaling\n        implementation remain follow-ons.\n      reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Own QA orchestration and separate qa-jira publication; helpers retain no transition\n        authority.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Use current review/PR/requirements receipts; no observation overlap, catch-up or replay\n        of completed mutations. Preserve full partial ledger on failure.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Human-only non-runtime PR targets need no invented deployment; environment-dependent\n        work still requires the trusted current deployment receipt.\n# Testing Strategy\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed\n      customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Prescribed isolated fixture set for all cases below; each case states its input and\n        expected outcome. All unmentioned snapshot facts are complete/valid and no earlier-priority\n        work exists.\n      initial_state: Fresh per case; only explicitly sequenced actions share state. Providers/tool\n        receipts are simulated, credentials dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Executable local fixtures and exact commands for all human cases below, bound to the PR\n        revision.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-08-H01\n        - R1-08-H02\n        - R1-08-H03\n      preserves:\n        - All case inputs, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup. No live provider data or\n          changed test expectations.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which the currently\n      approved automated QA skills do not execute. Human reviewers run these cases; developer CI and\n      PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-08-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n        prerequisites:\n          - Scripted native Story and Bug mixed API-child/database/UI plans with declared binding\n            and screenshots.\n        steps:\n          - Execute the prepared dispatch sequence.\n          - Inspect full nested ledger and human_pending.\n          - Inspect verified publication and transition order.\n        expected:\n          - Each step once, correct earlier-output binding, full evidence; Human Review only after\n            verified current-revision completion.\n        evidence:\n          - ordered tool audit, screenshots and typed ledger; tested PR revision and exact command.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-08-H02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC4\n          - TAC2\n        prerequisites:\n          - Observation schedules for until_expected/all_observations plus overrun, defect, missing\n            access and known upstream defect transcripts.\n        steps:\n          - Run each observation schedule against scripted outcomes.\n          - Inspect dispatch times, final ledger and destination.\n        expected:\n          - No overlap/catch-up; expected success/failure policy; overrun/inability blocks, known\n            defect queues; unfinished work explicitly NOT_RUN.\n        evidence:\n          - timestamped dispatch audit and result records; tested PR revision and exact command.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-08-H03\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Complete human-only native Bug static PR plan, rejected Task/Epic types, plus changed\n            source/requirements and unknown publication variants.\n        steps:\n          - Execute zero-AI QA.\n          - Repeat with each invalid variant.\n        expected:\n          - Zero AI cases and exact pending human list; no human PASS, no invented environment;\n            stale/unknown effects stop without replay.\n        evidence:\n          - tool audit and human handoff; tested PR revision and exact command.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live\n              records/resources.\n  automated_regression: Entrypoint contract tests for ordered complete ledgers, observation bounds,\n    all-human handoff and failure destinations.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
