            "description": "Owner approved implementation on 15 November 2026. R1-12 in the Pig Boss release-one set. No activation is authorized.\n\nReviewed role amendment and dependency additions authorized by the Director on 16 November 2026. Original criteria/cases and native status are retained; exact-base implementation gates remain.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: Offline decisions are useful only if the operator can compare them with complete current Jira facts. Filtered\n  searches must not make occupied work disappear.\nprerequisites:\n- ticket: PGB-81\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-99\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-145\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-148\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-162\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n- ticket: PGB-163\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n- id: AC1\n  requirement: One canonical configuration supplies site/projects, repositories, native mappings, actors, labels, bounds and\n    secret references; work text cannot override it.\n- id: AC2\n  requirement: The live read-only preview gathers complete bounded pages, unions current membership/dependencies/lineage with\n    supplied retained IDs and fresh-reads each known issue.\n- id: AC3\n  requirement: Missing pages, denied/deleted IDs, changed membership or exhausted budgets yield precise incomplete/hold results\n    rather than empty availability.\n- id: AC4\n  requirement: It resolves typed receipts through the supported provider representation and shows selections without writing\n    Jira or operational state.\n- id: AC5\n  requirement: Live preview resolves each project mapping and allowed cross-project prerequisites; project identity uses immutable\n    IDs and incomplete shared inventory never yields free capacity.\n- id: AC-ROLE1\n  requirement: The live preview composes complete scheduling declarations and recorded proof against exact current native/configured/retained\n    identity, explicitly reporting that worker execution and external PR freshness were not checked.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own Jira read adapter/config validation; retained IDs are supplied through the state interface when installed,\n      not an editable second customer configuration.\n    out_of_scope:\n    - Plexus/customer code changes\n    - Archived runtime reuse\n    - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n  - id: D03\n    decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n    reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n  - id: D04\n    decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label; equal labels in different\n      projects are independent. One customer installation supports multiple projects. Basic manager health is in release one;\n      worker monitoring and scaling implementation remain follow-ons.\n    reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  - id: D-ROLE\n    decision: Owner10906 assigns Pig Boss complete deterministic scheduling and recorded-proof checks; workers retain current\n      applicable execution proof.\n    reference: https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-144?focusedCommentId=10906\n  - id: D-PREP\n    decision: Director10909 permits in-stage current fact preparation from existing authority; only the implementer fills\n      declared mechanical slots and every action requires its applicable proof.\n    reference: https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-144?focusedCommentId=10909\n  constraints:\n  - id: TAC1\n    requirement: Own Jira read adapter/config validation; retained IDs are supplied through the state interface when installed,\n      not an editable second customer configuration.\n  - id: TAC2\n    requirement: Use configured HTTPS origins, verified TLS, bounded time/requests and no credential-bearing redirects; logs/diagnostics\n      exclude secrets and ticket contents.\n  - id: TAC3\n    requirement: Initial operator verification of complete service-account visibility is a prerequisite; searches cannot prove\n      unseen issues do not exist.\n  - id: TAC-ROLE1\n    requirement: Use the selected supported package/configuration and snapshot v2 profile without manager execution-context\n      or external PR/evidence prerequisites; retain complete native lineage, retained identity and uncertainty guards.\n  - id: TAC-ROLE2\n    requirement: Publish supported initial defaults from the prescribed finite source/copied fixture evidence, including count/byte/time\n      bounds and limits; do not claim every parser maximum or a live customer environment is supported.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n  - id: DATA-01\n    description: Prescribed isolated fixture set for all cases below; each case states its input and expected outcome. All\n      unmentioned snapshot facts are complete/valid and no earlier-priority work exists.\n    initial_state: Fresh per case; only explicitly sequenced actions share state. Providers/tool receipts are simulated, credentials\n      dummy.\n    reference: null\n    preparation_id: PREP-01\n    owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n  - id: PREP-01\n    owner: implementer\n    supplies: Executable local fixtures and exact commands for all human cases below, bound to the PR revision.\n    used_by:\n    - DATA-01\n    - R1-12-H01\n    - R1-12-H02\n    - R1-12-H03\n    - R1-12-H04\n    - R1-12-H05\n    preserves:\n    - All case inputs, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup. No live provider data or changed test expectations.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which the currently approved automated QA skills\n      do not execute. Human reviewers run these cases; developer CI and PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n    - id: R1-12-H01\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC1\n      - AC2\n      - AC4\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Recorded authorized Jira REST fixture pages and known IDs, including Human Review/Blocked work omitted by a ready-only\n        search; token is a dummy test value.\n      steps:\n      - Run against the scripted HTTP fixture server with canonical test config.\n      - Inspect exact known-ID/comment reads and decision.\n      expected:\n      - Complete pages and fresh known IDs used; full occupancy retained; zero write calls and matching offline decision.\n      evidence:\n      - command/output transcript and fixture before/after diff; tested PR revision and exact command.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live records/resources.\n    - id: R1-12-H02\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC2\n      - AC3\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Missing page, 403/404, rate limit, response timeout, relabelled known ticket and exceeded request/time/count fixtures.\n      steps:\n      - Run each fixture through preview.\n      - Inspect scope/diagnostic and call count.\n      expected:\n      - No fabricated free stream, no retries beyond the explicit read budget, no writes; shared unknown holds entire scan.\n      evidence:\n      - command/output transcript and fixture before/after diff; tested PR revision and exact command.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live records/resources.\n    - id: R1-12-H03\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC1\n      - TAC2\n      prerequisites:\n      - Unauthorized project/repository, credential URL, redirected request and deliberately secret-bearing provider error.\n      steps:\n      - Validate config and run each blocked transport fixture.\n      - Search output for the dummy secret and customer body.\n      expected:\n      - Invalid destination denied before credential send; no sensitive values in output.\n      evidence:\n      - redacted transport audit and output inspection; tested PR revision and exact command.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build output; do not change live records/resources.\n    - id: R1-12-H04\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC5\n      prerequisites:\n      - Two project IDs with different status/type mappings, equal labels, a cross-project prerequisite, renamed key, denied-project\n        and isolated-stream-conflict variants.\n      - Current PR checkout; prepared local simulated provider data; no live customer actions.\n      steps:\n      - Preview all variants through the simulated Jira adapter.\n      - Compare mapped stages, dependency results, native IDs and mutation trace.\n      expected:\n      - Correct mapping and prerequisite checks across projects; key rename preserves identity; known isolated conflict holds\n        only affected scope; denied project with unknown shared impact holds all writes; no preview mutations.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested PR revision, exact prepared commands/fixtures and sanitized outputs.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain evidence then remove disposable fixture/build output; no live changes.\n    - id: R1-12-H05\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC-ROLE1\n      - TAC-ROLE1\n      - TAC-ROLE2\n      prerequisites:\n      - Original H01–H04 fixture packet plus complete mixed/all-human scheduling and recorded repair inputs from PGB-163 without\n        manager execution context or external PR observations.\n      - Independent PGB-162 expected decisions; isolated current-requirement/root/mixed-profile failures and hidden external-change-only\n        control.\n      steps:\n      - Run the source and installed live preview and compare with the prescribed offline decisions.\n      - Run each role control and the candidate initial-default profile against this same finite packet; inspect count/byte/time\n        limits and evidence.\n      expected:\n      - Valid complete inputs match offline selections without writes; changed relevant proof holds and mixed profiles reject.\n        Hidden external changes are not claimed detected or execution-ready.\n      - Supported initial defaults name the verified finite envelope and bounds; the result claims neither support for every\n        parser maximum nor untested live customer acceptance.\n      evidence:\n      - Exact tested revision/pin, prepared commands, sanitized source/copied/offline comparison and bounded count/byte/time\n        results; separate simulated from actual evidence.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n  automated_regression: HTTP-fixture integration tests for complete inventory, fresh reads, request budgets and credential\n    boundaries.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
