            "description": "Owner-authorized same-scope split of PGB-85 on 15 November 2026. R1-29 in the Pig Boss release-one set. No activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: An uncertain Jira transition cannot be settled safely from its\n  current status or history alone. The manager needs to retain the exact request\n  and its original response so an operator can inspect what is known without\n  repeating the request.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-84\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A trusted writer can retain a verified publication reference and\n      prepare one transition capture for the matching pending attempt;\n      inspection shows its identity, request commitment and whether a response\n      was received.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: A trusted writer can save the original completed response once, and\n      inspection after restart preserves it without changing the pending outcome\n      or calling Jira.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Stale revisions, changed references, duplicate capture or response,\n      disabled writer controls and exceeded record limits cannot overwrite proof\n      or grant permission to send again; uncertain persistence remains explicit.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own original transition-proof persistence and inspection in the\n      production state adapter, bounded attempt contract, local conformance\n      driver and guide; PGB-85 owns reconciliation and PGB-87 owns the future\n      Jira sender.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer code changes\n      - Archived runtime reuse\n      - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery\n        and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n    - id: D03\n      decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n      reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n    - id: D04\n      decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID\n        + full label; equal labels in different projects are independent. One\n        customer installation supports multiple projects. Basic manager health\n        is in release one; worker monitoring and scaling implementation remain\n        follow-ons.\n      reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Use the existing four-record v1 store, ten agreed scalar capture\n        keys and conditional installation, stream and attempt revisions;\n        preserve unrelated fields within the existing 16-key and 32 KiB limits.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Retain verified publication before pointer publication, then\n        prepare capture before sending; bind the exact transition request and\n        publication observations to the immutable attempt identity, and save\n        only its original response.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Do not add a store, raw request or response bodies, imported\n        operator proof, a send/retry command, or a finalization bypass; missing\n        or unsupported proof stays distinguishable from rejection.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local\n      fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Prescribed isolated fixture set for all cases below; each case\n        states its input and expected outcome. All unmentioned snapshot facts\n        are complete/valid and no earlier-priority work exists.\n      initial_state: Fresh per case; only explicitly sequenced actions share state.\n        Providers/tool receipts are simulated, credentials dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Executable local fixtures and exact commands for all human cases\n        below, bound to the PR revision.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-29-H01\n        - R1-29-H02\n      preserves:\n        - All case inputs, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup. No\n          live provider data or changed test expectations.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which\n      the currently approved automated QA skills do not execute. Human reviewers\n      run these cases; developer CI and PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n      - execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        evidence:\n          - Command/output transcript, exact tested PR revision, fixture\n            before/after state and provider call audit.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build\n              output; do not change live records/resources.\n        id: R1-29-H01\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n        prerequisites:\n          - Two fresh pending-attempt fixtures with verified publication\n            observations, dummy credentials and simulated providers; final\n            inspection uses the actual PGB-83/84 composition.\n          - Implementer supplies exact local driver commands and fixture inputs\n            bound to the PR revision.\n        steps:\n          - Retain the verified publication reference and prepare capture.\n          - Inspect prepared-only state, then record the original 204 response\n            in one fixture and 409 in the other.\n          - Restart and inspect readable and JSON output.\n        expected:\n          - Matching proof is retained once; the same attempt and outcome remain\n            pending; unrelated fields are preserved.\n          - Zero Jira mutations or worker calls; prepared-only and\n            completed-response states are distinguishable.\n      - execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        evidence:\n          - Command/output transcript, exact tested PR revision, fixture\n            before/after state and provider call audit.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence then remove disposable local fixtures/build\n              output; do not change live records/resources.\n        id: R1-29-H02\n        requirements:\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - \"Fresh fixture per variant: stale revision, changed retained\n            reference, duplicate preparation, duplicate response, disabled\n            writer controls, exceeded extension capacity, exceeded record-size\n            limit, and persistence failure before or after a write.\"\n        steps:\n          - Run each prescribed operation once.\n          - Restart and inspect the same attempt and provider audit.\n        expected:\n          - Conflicts or bounded failures cannot overwrite proof.\n          - Uncertain writes may be absent or durably present; neither result\n            authorizes resending or finalizes the pending attempt.\n          - No live records, Jira mutations or worker calls.\n  automated_regression: Production-adapter and command tests for exact\n    request/publication binding, one-time persistence, revision fences, record\n    limits and inspect-after-uncertainty behavior.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
