            "description": "This same-scope prerequisite delivers three independently usable prepared inputs before the full PGB-132 suite. It does not execute helpers or inherit PGB-132’s evidence exception.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: Developers and QA reviewers need a complete mixed QA input handoff and honest\n  missing-parameter and stale-deployment controls before the larger preparation suite is available.\n  Existing fixed controls do not yet isolate those two required-input boundaries.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-74\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-76\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-77\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-108\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-110\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A developer can create and inspect a fresh private mixed Story input packet with the\n      selected request, extraction mapping, SQL parameters, UI checkpoints and exact consumer\n      bindings.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: The separate missing reviewed parameter-count and stale-deployment controls expose\n      those precise boundaries without contradictory proof, guessed inputs or changed work\n      expectations.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Preparation preserves existing publication fixtures, creates empty execution outputs\n      and explains input inspection, authority requirements and safe cleanup without claiming helper\n      execution or live readiness.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Deliver the existing source-only prepareQaFixture dispatch-inputs command with\n      I01-story, I02-parameters and I11-stale-environment, their regression coverage, current\n      producer/reviewer guidance and publication metadata in one PR.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer code changes\n      - Archived runtime reuse\n      - Activation, worker monitoring, Cursor deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n    - id: D03\n      decision: Story writing and human-invoked request-rework are separate skills.\n      reference: docs/architecture/manager-human-rework.md\n    - id: D04\n      decision: Pig Boss is the manager. A stream is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label; equal\n        labels in different projects are independent. One customer installation supports multiple\n        projects. Basic manager health is in release one; worker monitoring and scaling\n        implementation remain follow-ons.\n      reference: docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Reuse existing raw-work/context, receipt validators, fixture module and\n        helper/publisher contracts without a new schema, engine, provider adapter or installed\n        skill.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Keep supplied/mock facts and operator guidance separate from actual output and\n        authority; preserve current-review and artifact/actor/tenant/PR bindings and withhold any\n        expected terminal result.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Use a fresh private absolute folder, exclusive writes and artifact hashes; keep default\n        publication preparation unchanged and never overwrite retained evidence.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed\n      customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: The three fixed supplied/mock inputs I01-story, I02-parameters and\n        I11-stale-environment, produced in a fresh private folder.\n      initial_state: Fresh per case; only explicitly sequenced actions share state. Providers/tool\n        receipts are simulated, credentials dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: The exact source-only preparation command, three complete fixed input packets and existing\n        read-only validation/inspection commands for R1-30-H01 through R1-30-H03, bound to the\n        reviewed source revision.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-30-H01\n        - R1-30-H02\n        - R1-30-H03\n      preserves:\n        - All case inputs, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup. No live provider data or\n          changed test expectations.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/IaC or instruction contracts, which the currently\n      approved automated QA skills do not execute. Human reviewers run these cases; developer CI and\n      PR review remain required.\n    cases:\n      - execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain commands, input hashes and inspection evidence first; remove only the owned\n              disposable preparation root. No live resources are created.\n        id: R1-30-H01\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Reviewed same-release source checkout with its already prepared validator dependencies;\n            a fresh absolute private output path; dummy supplied/mock data only.\n        steps:\n          - Run the delivered source-only preparation command and record source revision, module\n            hash and emitted input hashes.\n          - Inspect I01-story raw work, separate context, current-review predecessors, child\n            ownership, request/assertions, extraction pointer, SQL layout and three UI\n            image/checkpoint bindings.\n          - Verify the existing raw-work and predecessor checks, empty output directory and\n            NOT_READY authority/capability notice; repeat the command only against the same occupied\n            path to verify refusal without overwriting files.\n        expected:\n          - Exactly the three declared variants are listed, with complete retrievable inputs and\n            matching hashes.\n          - The baseline has valid declared work/context and coherent current proof; extraction\n            values remain unbound until actual helper evidence exists.\n          - No helper, timer, provider or publisher is run; no assessment, verdict or current\n            terminal is supplied, and original files survive the occupied-path refusal.\n        evidence:\n          - Exact source command, revision and hashes, validator output, artifact/consumer\n            inspection and before/after occupied-path file hashes.\n      - execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain commands, input hashes and inspection evidence first; remove only the owned\n              disposable preparation root. No live resources are created.\n        id: R1-30-H02\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Fresh generated I01-story and I02-parameters inputs from the reviewed source and\n            existing read-only work/receipt validators.\n        steps:\n          - Compare raw work, query, parameter array and bindings with the baseline.\n          - Inspect the matching DB operation in facts.yaml and predecessor requirement context,\n            then run existing read-only start/predecessor validation.\n          - Retain the diagnostic and inspect that no supplied expected value repairs the missing\n            trusted count or populates output.\n        expected:\n          - The named negative keeps original work expectations and differs at the required reviewed\n            DB parameter_count, which is null in both trusted-context copies.\n          - Start validation rejects with DATABASE_PARAMETERS at the DB parameter boundary;\n            predecessor validation exposes the same missing-count cause.\n          - The baseline remains valid and the optional null parameter sidecar is not claimed as the\n            rejection cause.\n        evidence:\n          - Raw positive/negative inputs, context comparison, exact parser/receipt diagnostics and\n            empty output listing.\n      - execution: human\n        owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: human QA reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain commands, input hashes and inspection evidence first; remove only the owned\n              disposable preparation root. No live resources are created.\n        id: R1-30-H03\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - Fresh generated I01-story and I11-stale-environment inputs; current review/PR facts and\n            original mock pipeline comments are available.\n        steps:\n          - Match each environment receipt to its original pipeline comment by URI, comment ID,\n            repository and PR number.\n          - Parse the original comment body and compare source/deployed revision with normalized\n            proof and current review/PR.\n          - Compare the baseline and inspect preserved actor, target, readiness, original\n            publication input bytes and empty output.\n        expected:\n          - Stale receipt and original comment source/deployed revision agree with each other and\n            differ from current reviewed PR; no current pipeline body contradicts that stale claim.\n          - The baseline remains current, all other proof identities stay consistent, and the\n            negative is visibly unsuitable as current deployment proof.\n          - Inspection does not assert a helper/publisher runtime result, human acceptance of\n            PGB-132 or live deployment readiness.\n        evidence:\n          - Receipt/original-comment/current-PR comparison, positive-control comparison,\n            preservation hashes and input/output listings.\n  automated_regression: Use the existing emitted-input tests and raw-work/receipt validators to check\n    the mixed handoff, exact missing trusted count, coherent stale proof, artifact hashes and\n    preserved empty outputs/default publication fixtures.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
