            "description": "Current delivery split (16 November2026): R1-36 / PGB-150 delivers the complete source inspection library and importable fixture API. PGB-147 retains its full acceptance contract and introduces the runnable fixture CLI, installed-runtime delivery and source/copied acceptance. PGB-145 remains a prerequisite and is delivered. PGB-147 is Blocked, waiting on PGB-150 / PR #112 to merge to main and Director's explicit release. Its seven-file checkpoint is archived and parked, not actively implementing; comment 10884 records the exact checkpoint. This dependency wait is not a PGB-147 defect and does not mark acceptance, merge or activation complete. The earlier publication preface and YAML comments below are retained as historical text, not current delivery gates.\n\nProvisional — not ready for delivery. R1-33 in the Pig Boss release-one set. Preparation draft only; no activation is authorized. Actual reviewed/merged PGB-145 rebind and Director publication gates remain.\n\n```yaml\n# Provisional — not ready for delivery. No Jira publication or implementation is authorized by this draft.\n# Native title: Inspect named Jira issues safely\n# Source identity: reserved R1-33; native parent Epic PGB-66. Native key is not allocated here.\n# Reviewed plan SHA256: 858c3e8d02a8ae0b3cd810f1e2e00a70dedcd3515cfe18f415a98ef0828f3cb4\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\n\n# Problem to solve\nproblem_to_solve: An authorized caller cannot inspect the native issues and comments needed to\n  diagnose a manager input. It needs current observations and explicit incomplete results without\n  first running a scheduler or discovering a whole project.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-145\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n  - ticket: PGB-150\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A documented source/copied library call inspects the supplied immutable issue IDs,\n      their fixed assignment properties, complete comment pages and named exact comments.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: Results identify complete, unavailable and changed observations, retain successful\n      observations, and distinguish an unknown pointer from a confirmed value.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Invalid inputs fail before credential resolution; requests use the fixed HTTPS gateway,\n      verified TLS, no redirects or retries, and finite count/byte/time limits.\n  - id: AC4\n    requirement: Safe human/JSON harness reports show requested completeness, counters and recovery\n      without credentials or raw bodies; every result says domain discovery and admission are not\n      evaluated.\n  - id: AC5\n    requirement: The same prescribed inspection works through actual copied dependencies from an\n      unrelated directory, with honest setup failure and no source fallback.\n\n# Technical Acceptance Criteria\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Own fixed read-only native issue inspection, its source/copied library and fixture\n      harness, distribution, tests, documentation and publication metadata.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - Plexus/customer repository changes, AWS resolver/wrapper, State adapter and\n        operational-state writes.\n      - Receipt acceptance, policy selection/admission, external PR/evidence fetching, a new input\n        producer or a PGB-144 proof-policy decision.\n      - Production live CLI, provider probes, deployment, activation, worker monitoring, Cursor\n        deduplication, automatic recovery and new QA engines.\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions: []\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Repository `danielchappell/Pigboard`, base `main`, one PR; own the fixed native\n        read/inspection library, test harness, distribution and its docs/metadata only.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Consume PGB-145's canonical validated connection/bounds and trusted programmatic\n        resolver; expose no arbitrary URL, JQL, method, transport module, credential CLI flag,\n        environment override or insecure mode.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Preserve native IDs/server metadata and endpoint-specific comment pagination; generic\n        404, missing pages and visibility limits cannot prove absence.\n    - id: TAC4\n      requirement: Count all attempted requests and bytes, bound private observations as well as public\n        reports, cancel owned I/O and fence late resolver results; return no scheduling or semantic\n        receipt proof.\n\n# Testing Strategy\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout, actual prepared copied runtime and disposable local\n      HTTPS fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Prescribed isolated B1 fixture set for the four human groups below, including only\n        their listed finite variants and controls.\n      initial_state: Fresh per variant; only explicitly paired controls share their stated sequence.\n        Provider responses are scripted and credentials are dummy.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: PR-bound executable local HTTPS fixture scripts, literal reports and permitted request\n        traces, exact source/copied commands and prepared absolute paths for every listed variant;\n        all expected answers are authored independently of the production collector.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-33-H01\n        - R1-33-H02\n        - R1-33-H03\n        - R1-33-H04\n      preserves:\n        - All acceptance criteria, technical constraints, case inputs, finite variants and limits,\n          paired controls, order, expected outcomes, evidence and cleanup.\n        - Existing source/copied distinction, verified TLS and no-effects boundaries; no live\n          provider data, changed expectations, new cases or raised budgets.\n        - \"All original PGB-82 acceptance remains on final82: five AC, three TAC and four human\n          groups, including full integrated preview and offline-equivalent policy results.\"\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI/library contracts, which the currently approved\n      automated QA skills do not execute. QA skills are []; human reviewers run the prescribed\n      cases. Developer regressions, CI and independent PR review remain required and do not count as\n      human acceptance.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-33-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC4\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the PR-bound local fixture packet DATA-01, exact commands, literal\n            expected reports and maximum permitted call traces before execution; do not generate\n            expected answers from the production collector.\n          - Prepared Node and root validator dependencies, source checkout and actual copied\n            runtime; fresh disposable data per variant, dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS\n            fixture servers. No live Jira account, AWS, Postman or UI is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: complete, empty-comments, renamed-key,\n            unknown-pointer, exact-mismatch. Each uses fresh state except its explicitly paired\n            controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - For each listed variant, run the prepared source command using node\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs --case R1-33-H01 --variant NAME --runtime\n            SOURCE_ROOT --json; PREP-01 supplies each exact variant name and absolute prepared root.\n          - Compare the report and permitted request audit with the literal expectations below;\n            inspect actual counters, bytes, elapsed time and cleanup.\n          - Repeat the same variant through the actual copied runtime from an unrelated working\n            directory, using the copied harness and --runtime COPIED_ROOT; PREP-01 supplies the\n            exact copied command and absolute root.\n          - Inspect no-effects and cancellation evidence and compare source/input/server\n            before-and-after hashes. Where the guide-and-install variant prescribes readable output,\n            also run its human form without --json and compare its meaning with JSON.\n        expected:\n          - \"complete: two issues, one present pointer each, two comment pages plus one named exact\n            target, literal IDs/metadata and requested complete/domain false. empty-comments:\n            explicit zero-total page, present pointer. renamed-key: same ID/current key.\n            unknown-pointer: pointer404 yields incomplete/POINTER_UNKNOWN, never null.\n            exact-mismatch: changed exact body/metadata yields CHANGED_INPUT.\"\n          - Every result reports inspection_scope requested_issues, domain_complete false, admission\n            not_evaluated and receipt_proof not_evaluated; requested completeness never certifies\n            the whole domain.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested PR revision, source/copied runtime identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            source/copied commands.\n          - Command/output transcripts, exit codes, safe reports and literal expected-report\n            comparison.\n          - Permitted request trace, actual request/count/byte/time measurements,\n            no-effects/cancellation observations and before/after hashes.\n          - Cleanup result and any remaining unverified outcome; these local fixture observations do\n            not prove live Jira, AWS, supported production capacity or activation.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the evidence packet and close the prescribed local fixture servers, sockets and\n              timers; the resolver-late fixture stops and acknowledges its own I/O where that\n              variant applies.\n            - Remove only disposable fixture/build directories and damaged copies; preserve the\n              usable prepared release, source and retained evidence. Do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-33-H02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC3\n          - TAC4\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the PR-bound local fixture packet DATA-01, exact commands, literal\n            expected reports and maximum permitted call traces before execution; do not generate\n            expected answers from the production collector.\n          - Prepared Node and root validator dependencies, source checkout and actual copied\n            runtime; fresh disposable data per variant, dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS\n            fixture servers. No live Jira account, AWS, Postman or UI is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: missing-page, changed-total, duplicate-comment,\n            zero-progress, issue403, issue404, rate429, header-timeout, body-timeout,\n            resolver-reject, resolver-abort, resolver-late. Each uses fresh state except its\n            explicitly paired controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - For each listed variant, run the prepared source command using node\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs --case R1-33-H02 --variant NAME --runtime\n            SOURCE_ROOT --json; PREP-01 supplies each exact variant name and absolute prepared root.\n          - Compare the report and permitted request audit with the literal expectations below;\n            inspect actual counters, bytes, elapsed time and cleanup.\n          - Repeat the same variant through the actual copied runtime from an unrelated working\n            directory, using the copied harness and --runtime COPIED_ROOT; PREP-01 supplies the\n            exact copied command and absolute root.\n          - Inspect no-effects and cancellation evidence and compare source/input/server\n            before-and-after hashes. Where the guide-and-install variant prescribes readable output,\n            also run its human form without --json and compare its meaning with JSON.\n        expected:\n          - \"missing-page, changed-total, duplicate-comment, zero-progress, issue403, issue404,\n            rate429, header-timeout, body-timeout, resolver-reject, resolver-abort, resolver-late:\n            each has a literal stop point/code; no retry, swallowed secret, false absence or\n            post-return B-owned read. Late resolver case expects cancel_unconfirmed and discards the\n            late dummy token; fixture itself acknowledges/stops its own I/O during cleanup.\"\n          - Every result reports inspection_scope requested_issues, domain_complete false, admission\n            not_evaluated and receipt_proof not_evaluated; requested completeness never certifies\n            the whole domain.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested PR revision, source/copied runtime identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            source/copied commands.\n          - Command/output transcripts, exit codes, safe reports and literal expected-report\n            comparison.\n          - Permitted request trace, actual request/count/byte/time measurements,\n            no-effects/cancellation observations and before/after hashes.\n          - Cleanup result and any remaining unverified outcome; these local fixture observations do\n            not prove live Jira, AWS, supported production capacity or activation.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the evidence packet and close the prescribed local fixture servers, sockets and\n              timers; the resolver-late fixture stops and acknowledges its own I/O where that\n              variant applies.\n            - Remove only disposable fixture/build directories and damaged copies; preserve the\n              usable prepared release, source and retained evidence. Do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-33-H03\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC3\n          - AC4\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC4\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the PR-bound local fixture packet DATA-01, exact commands, literal\n            expected reports and maximum permitted call traces before execution; do not generate\n            expected answers from the production collector.\n          - Prepared Node and root validator dependencies, source checkout and actual copied\n            runtime; fresh disposable data per variant, dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS\n            fixture servers. No live Jira account, AWS, Postman or UI is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: invalid-origin, invalid-request, out-of-scope-issue,\n            redirect, untrusted-ca, wrong-host, error-canary, compressed-response, known-limit,\n            comment-limit, page-limit, request-limit, response-byte-limit, total-byte-limit,\n            request-time-limit, scan-time-limit. Each uses fresh state except its explicitly paired\n            controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - For each listed variant, run the prepared source command using node\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs --case R1-33-H03 --variant NAME --runtime\n            SOURCE_ROOT --json; PREP-01 supplies each exact variant name and absolute prepared root.\n          - Compare the report and permitted request audit with the literal expectations below;\n            inspect actual counters, bytes, elapsed time and cleanup.\n          - Repeat the same variant through the actual copied runtime from an unrelated working\n            directory, using the copied harness and --runtime COPIED_ROOT; PREP-01 supplies the\n            exact copied command and absolute root.\n          - Inspect no-effects and cancellation evidence and compare source/input/server\n            before-and-after hashes. Where the guide-and-install variant prescribes readable output,\n            also run its human form without --json and compare its meaning with JSON.\n        expected:\n          - invalid-origin, invalid-request, out-of-scope-issue, redirect, untrusted-ca, wrong-host,\n            error-canary, compressed-response. Invalid setup invokes no resolver; rejected scope has\n            no follow-up body/comment reads; redirect target receives no credentials/request; TLS\n            failures occur; reports exclude every body/token/reference/error canary.\n          - \"L01 known-limit: two supplied issues, max_known_issues1 then2. B1 rejects pre-resolver\n            at1; at2 continues.\"\n          - \"L02 comment-limit: two ordinary comments, max_comments1 then2. B1 incomplete before\n            retaining excess; at2 complete.\"\n          - \"L03 page-limit: two comment pages, max_pages1 then2. B1 stops before requesting second\n            at1.\"\n          - \"L04 request-limit: a literal four-request single-issue script, max_requests3 then4,\n            max_pages1. B1 stops before fourth at3; at4 completes.\"\n          - \"L05 response-byte-limit: one identity-encoded body with literal byte lengthN, capN−1\n            thenN. B1 aborts at excess; no raw/error disclosure.\"\n          - \"L06 total-byte-limit: two responses with literal lengths summingN, per-response\n            cap≤N−1, totalN−1 thenN. B1 counts both and stops at aggregate excess; private\n            observation serialization has a separate deterministic oversized-projection subvariant\n            within this case.\"\n          - \"L07 request-time-limit: fixture withholds headers/body past fixed request deadline;\n            paired immediate response. B1 cancels actual socket, no later B-owned work. Deadline is\n            not increased to force a pass.\"\n          - \"L08 scan-time-limit: resolver plus two individually timely responses exceed total\n            deadline; paired immediate sequence. B1 total includes resolution, parsing and cleanup;\n            result incomplete even if last parse otherwise succeeds.\"\n          - Each budget-hit input changes only the named budget to one below its independently known\n            demand while preserving A’s cross-field relations; run its paired positive-at-limit\n            control. Expected demand and call counts are literal fixture facts prepared before\n            execution. Do not raise bounds after observing failure.\n          - Every result reports inspection_scope requested_issues, domain_complete false, admission\n            not_evaluated and receipt_proof not_evaluated; requested completeness never certifies\n            the whole domain.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested PR revision, source/copied runtime identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            source/copied commands.\n          - Command/output transcripts, exit codes, safe reports and literal expected-report\n            comparison.\n          - Permitted request trace, actual request/count/byte/time measurements,\n            no-effects/cancellation observations and before/after hashes.\n          - Cleanup result and any remaining unverified outcome; these local fixture observations do\n            not prove live Jira, AWS, supported production capacity or activation.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the evidence packet and close the prescribed local fixture servers, sockets and\n              timers; the resolver-late fixture stops and acknowledges its own I/O where that\n              variant applies.\n            - Remove only disposable fixture/build directories and damaged copies; preserve the\n              usable prepared release, source and retained evidence. Do not change live\n              records/resources.\n      - id: R1-33-H04\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC4\n          - AC5\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the PR-bound local fixture packet DATA-01, exact commands, literal\n            expected reports and maximum permitted call traces before execution; do not generate\n            expected answers from the production collector.\n          - Prepared Node and root validator dependencies, source checkout and actual copied\n            runtime; fresh disposable data per variant, dummy token/reference and fixed local HTTPS\n            fixture servers. No live Jira account, AWS, Postman or UI is needed.\n          - \"Run exactly these named variants: guide-and-install, damaged-copy. Each uses fresh\n            state except its explicitly paired controls.\"\n          - The test-only harness audits the original fixed HTTPS origin/path/method before routing\n            to loopback HTTPS with explicit test CA and hostname; certificate and hostname checks\n            stay enabled. Production has no test origin, CA, transport, insecure mode or fixture\n            imports.\n        steps:\n          - For each listed variant, run the prepared source command using node\n            test/fixtures/jira-preview-harness.mjs --case R1-33-H04 --variant NAME --runtime\n            SOURCE_ROOT --json; PREP-01 supplies each exact variant name and absolute prepared root.\n          - Compare the report and permitted request audit with the literal expectations below;\n            inspect actual counters, bytes, elapsed time and cleanup.\n          - Repeat the same variant through the actual copied runtime from an unrelated working\n            directory, using the copied harness and --runtime COPIED_ROOT; PREP-01 supplies the\n            exact copied command and absolute root.\n          - Inspect no-effects and cancellation evidence and compare source/input/server\n            before-and-after hashes. Where the guide-and-install variant prescribes readable output,\n            also run its human form without --json and compare its meaning with JSON.\n        expected:\n          - \"guide-and-install: source/copied documented examples and human/JSON parity, actual\n            copied module/dependency hashes, unrelated cwd. damaged-copy: remove one required module\n            only in a disposable copy; expect safe setup failure, no source fallback/fetch/repair.\n            Other cases already run both routes; this group verifies installation/recovery rather\n            than adding a third matrix.\"\n          - Every result reports inspection_scope requested_issues, domain_complete false, admission\n            not_evaluated and receipt_proof not_evaluated; requested completeness never certifies\n            the whole domain.\n          - Library collection makes no Jira or operational-state writes. Keep successful\n            observations and explicit failures; do not turn missing evidence into a pass or start an\n            alternate fixture campaign.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested PR revision, source/copied runtime identity, fixture hashes and exact\n            source/copied commands.\n          - Command/output transcripts, exit codes, safe reports and literal expected-report\n            comparison.\n          - Permitted request trace, actual request/count/byte/time measurements,\n            no-effects/cancellation observations and before/after hashes.\n          - Cleanup result and any remaining unverified outcome; these local fixture observations do\n            not prove live Jira, AWS, supported production capacity or activation.\n        cleanup:\n         