            "description": "R1-38 in the Pig Boss release-one set. This native-only child corrects two demonstrated source observation defects in PGB-150. It targets the pinned source feature branch; PGB-145 is its only native completion prerequisite. Publication does not mean implementation, human acceptance, merge or activation.\n\n```yaml\n# Native title: Read native Jira observations accurately\n# Source identity: R1-38; native key assigned only by actual create/readback.\n# Reviewed repair plan SHA256: 53ed8317173824d822e2c55f3030837f1ac1e02785228d4470e0bff4b26a789c\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: A caller inspecting a visible issue currently loses its pointer and comments when\n  its description is empty. The same caller can receive a false changed-input failure when Jira\n  returns an unchanged comment with a different JSON member order. Both failures prevent a truthful\n  bounded inspection.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-145\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: A named issue with an explicit null description retains that absence and completes its\n      requested pointer, comment-page and exact-comment reads when those responses are otherwise\n      valid. A missing description remains a response-shape failure.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: An exact comment with the same JSON body value and server metadata completes even when\n      root or nested object members arrive in a different order. A changed content-array order or\n      existing metadata mismatch remains CHANGED_INPUT; an unmatched exact value is not retained as\n      accepted.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: The safe report, private observation boundary, limits, partial-result behavior and\n      cleanup remain intact. The source guide explains empty descriptions and semantic comment\n      comparison without claiming valid work, complete domain inventory or installed delivery.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: codex/pgb150-source-inspection\n    change_boundary: One eight-path child PR corrects explicit null issue descriptions and semantic\n      exact-comment comparison in the pinned PGB-150 source feature. It adds four finite source\n      regressions, guide and native-only publication support; no source Story is composed.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - No customer repository, installed bundle, manager state, policy, admission, proof, provider\n        probe, activation or new transport/credential path.\n      - No fixture packet JSON/TLS/harness rewrite, source contract-count change or production\n        parser format change.\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions: []\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Repository danielchappell/Pigboard; this native child targets the pinned PGB-150 source\n        feature branch at 95c711999b90b20842dfd172f7966f73c8cfde34 and owns exactly the eight\n        reviewed paths. PGB-145 is its sole native ai_qa_complete prerequisite; PGB-150 receives\n        this child as its own prerequisite.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Preserve inspectJiraIssues(configInput,{issue_ids,comment_targets},{resolveSecret}),\n        the existing string/null consumer shape, raw/private byte meanings, validation, credentials,\n        TLS, scope restrictions and no-effect controls. Correct only the demonstrated\n        issue-description normalization and exact-comment comparison sites.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Keep the existing 35-variant packet, eight controls and private-projection case\n        unchanged. Add only the four prescribed finite regression subcases through the existing\n        importable test fixture API with independent literal observations, counters, cleanup and\n        source/input/runtime preservation. Document current effort and native-only repair history\n        without claiming complete source/native inventory.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Pinned Pigboard PGB-150 source branch at 95c711999b90b20842dfd172f7966f73c8cfde34\n      with prepared Node dependencies and disposable local HTTPS fixtures; no live Jira or installed\n      runtime.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: \"Four literal source regression subcases: null-description, missing-description,\n        adf-nested-order and adf-array-change. The original 35 variants, eight controls and private\n        projection remain unchanged.\"\n      initial_state: Fresh dummy local HTTPS server and source-derived fixture per subcase. Only the named\n        response field/body member order changes from the guide-and-install input.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Reviewed PR-bound exact source import commands and four independently authored literal\n        expected safe/private reports, GET traces, wire/private byte counts and preservation hashes\n        from the sealed regression design; no oracle is derived from production output.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-38-H01\n        - R1-38-H02\n      preserves:\n        - Pinned PGB-150 source API, existing 35-variant/eight-control/private-projection packet,\n          fixed HTTPS/TLS, dummy secret resolver, count/byte/time limits and no-effect controls.\n        - Four named subcases and their exact literal values; no new provider run, raised bound,\n          test-only production hook, changed fixture packet JSON/TLS/harness or inferred acceptance.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: The currently approved automated QA skills do not execute this source library\n      and local HTTPS fixture contract. QA skills are []; two designated human groups remain NOT_RUN\n      until separately executed or dispositioned. Developer tests, independent QA, CI and code\n      review are separate.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-38-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies reviewed source import commands and independent literal oracles for\n            null-description and missing-description; use fresh dummy data and prepared\n            dependencies.\n          - No live Jira, provider, Postman, UI, installed runtime or dependency fetch is required.\n        steps:\n          - From the reviewed source checkout, run the null-description subcase through the\n            importable fixture API. Compare the retained issue body:null, four-read\n            issue→pointer→page→exact trace, complete phases, safe JSON, counters, zero effects and\n            cleanup.\n          - Run the missing-description control on fresh data. Compare the one-read RESPONSE_INVALID\n            stop, no retained issue and all later phases not_requested.\n          - Inspect source/input/runtime before-after hashes and record the exact revision, command,\n            outputs and cleanup.\n        expected:\n          - null-description completes four GETs with attempts/completed/failed 4/4/0, wire lengths\n            146+265+258+206=875 and private serialized bytes 1109. The issue body is literal null,\n            not an empty document; pointer, page and exact observations complete.\n          - missing-description fails after one issue GET with RESPONSE_INVALID, 127 received bytes,\n            zero retained observation bytes and no pointer/page/exact request. Both have\n            resolver_calls=1, effects=0, cleanup_complete and unchanged hashes.\n          - Safe JSON omits private bodies, retains inspection_scope\n            requested_issues/domain_complete false/admission and receipt_proof not_evaluated. Null\n            inventory is not valid startable work.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested child PR revision, pinned parent revision, exact import command, fixture and\n            prepared dependency identity.\n          - Safe report, private acquisition comparison, permitted GET trace, wire and private byte\n            counters, resolver/effects audit, before/after hashes and cleanup result.\n          - Any failed or unverified step with its actual stop point; local observations do not\n            establish live provider, installed-runtime or activation acceptance.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the PR revision, exact source invocation and literal comparison evidence. Close\n              local fixture servers, sockets and timers; verify cleanup_complete and unchanged\n              source/input/runtime hashes.\n            - Remove only disposable source-derived fixtures. Preserve the reviewed source, first\n              failure evidence and all retained results. No live Jira or operational-state changes.\n      - id: R1-38-H02\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies reviewed source import commands and independent literal oracles for\n            adf-nested-order and adf-array-change; use fresh dummy data and prepared dependencies.\n          - Retain original endpoint-specific ADF strings in private observations; do not rewrite\n            the packet or derive expected values from the reader.\n        steps:\n          - Run adf-nested-order through the importable fixture API. Compare root, paragraph and\n            text object member reordering with the same JSON value and metadata, distinct retained\n            endpoint strings, four-read trace, safe/private reports, counters and cleanup.\n          - Run adf-array-change on fresh data. Compare the B-then-A content array with the A-then-B\n            page value and confirm CHANGED_INPUT with no accepted exact comment.\n          - Inspect the unchanged existing exact-mismatch timestamp-sensitive case, zero effects and\n            source/input/runtime preservation; record revision, commands, outputs and cleanup.\n        expected:\n          - adf-nested-order completes with 4/4/0 GETs, wire lengths 181+265+344+292=1082 and\n            private serialized bytes 1370; same JSON value and metadata complete despite\n            object-member order. Both original body strings remain distinct and retained.\n          - adf-array-change is incomplete/CHANGED_INPUT after 4/4/0 GETs and the same 1082 wire\n            bytes; private serialized bytes are 1048. Earlier issue/pointer/page acquisition\n            remains; exact_comments is empty. Changed array order and real metadata mismatch remain\n            failures.\n          - Both have resolver_calls=1, effects=0, cleanup_complete and unchanged hashes. Safe JSON\n            omits private data and does not claim whole-domain inventory, proof or admission.\n        evidence:\n          - Tested child PR revision, pinned parent revision, exact import command, fixture and\n            prepared dependency identity.\n          - Safe report, private acquisition comparison, permitted GET trace, wire and private byte\n            counters, resolver/effects audit, before/after hashes and cleanup result.\n          - Any failed or unverified step with its actual stop point; local observations do not\n            establish live provider, installed-runtime or activation acceptance.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the PR revision, exact source invocation and literal comparison evidence. Close\n              local fixture servers, sockets and timers; verify cleanup_complete and unchanged\n              source/input/runtime hashes.\n            - Remove only disposable source-derived fixtures. Preserve the reviewed source, first\n              failure evidence and all retained results. No live Jira or operational-state changes.\n  automated_regression: Four finite source regressions with literal private/report/trace/counter\n    oracles; preserve the original 35 variants, eight controls and L06 private projection. Run the\n    bounded affected source selection and both publication guards. Hosted CI, independent QA and\n    designated human acceptance remain separate.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
