            "description": "R1-40 in the Pig Boss release-one set. This native-only child fixes a demonstrated duplicate-target validation defect in PGB-150. It uses the pinned parent code context; PGB-145 is its sole native completion prerequisite. Publication does not mean implementation, human acceptance, merge or activation.\n\n```yaml\n# Native title: Reject duplicate Jira comment targets\n# Source identity: provisional R1-40; actual native key assigned only by create/readback.\n# Reviewed plan SHA256: a479bb57472cabb565e34133fdecdc9923396223c1ba7db909c267b58f68bf8b\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: A source caller can request one exact Jira comment twice by reversing the two\n  target fields. The invalid request currently resolves credentials and performs duplicate reads\n  instead of stopping before provider access.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-145\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: \"Duplicate ticket/comment ID pairs are invalid regardless of object-member order:\n      report invalid/INPUT_INVALID before resolver invocation, Jira requests or private observation,\n      without mutating the input.\"\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: One unique target with reversed member order completes the same bounded native\n      inspection as before. Existing shape, membership, security, limits, private output and the\n      PGB-152 null/ADF corrections remain intact.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: The source guide states that target identity is the ticket/comment pair. Native-only\n      delivery records distinguish implemented behavior, dated publication facts and separate\n      verification, human acceptance and integration evidence.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: codex/pgb150-source-inspection\n    change_boundary: One eight-path native-only child PR fixes exact-comment target uniqueness in the\n      pinned PGB-150 feature; source Story counts stay unchanged.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - No customer repository, installed runtime, manager state, proof, policy, admission, live\n        provider, deployment or activation change.\n      - No generic parser, canonicalizer, new dependency, transport, credential path, fixture packet\n        rewrite or limit change.\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions: []\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Repository danielchappell/Pigboard; one eight-path child PR targets the pinned PGB-150\n        feature branch at 1524127c6d9ffbad8481cf7ce86bcc19cb712f52. PGB-145 is its sole native\n        ai_qa_complete prerequisite; PGB-150 adds this child as a prerequisite without losing\n        PGB-145 or PGB-152.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Preserve inspectJiraIssues and validation order. Compare the two already validated\n        string IDs as one fixed ordered pair; do not deduplicate, coerce, sort caller keys, change\n        membership, resolve a secret for invalid input or add a transport capability.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Preserve all 35 original fixture variants, eight controls, private projection and four\n        PGB-152 regression subcases. Add only the two finite source subcases through the existing\n        fixture API with independent literal reports, traces, counters, cleanup and preservation\n        checks.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Pinned PGB-150 feature branch at 1524127c6d9ffbad8481cf7ce86bcc19cb712f52 with\n      prepared Node dependencies and disposable local HTTPS fixtures; no live Jira or installed\n      runtime.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: \"Two source-derived guide-and-install subcases: duplicate-target-member-order and\n        unique-target-member-order. The original fixture packet and PGB-152 cases remain unchanged.\"\n      initial_state: Fresh dummy local HTTPS server per subcase. The negative adds a reordered duplicate\n        target and one unused exact reply; the positive reverses the sole target member order while\n        retaining the four original replies.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: Reviewed source import commands, prepared absolute root and independently authored literal\n        safe/private oracles, request traces, counters, preservation hashes and cleanup checks for\n        the two named subcases.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-40-H01\n      preserves:\n        - The original 35-variant packet, eight controls, private projection and four PGB-152 source\n          regression subcases.\n        - Fixed HTTPS/TLS, dummy trusted resolver, existing finite bounds, no-effect controls and\n          original guide acquisition. No provider run or oracle generated from production output.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: No approved automated QA skill executes this source library/local HTTPS fixture.\n      qa_skills are []; the one designated human group remains NOT_RUN until separately observed or\n      dispositioned. Developer tests, independent QA, CI and code review are separate.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-40-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the exact reviewed source command, dummy HTTPS fixtures and independent\n            literal oracles. Use fresh data and prepared dependencies.\n          - No live Jira, provider, Postman, UI, installed runtime or dependency fetch is required.\n        steps:\n          - Run duplicate-target-member-order with two targets for ticket_id 1000/comment_id 2001 in\n            reversed member order. Compare invalid/INPUT_INVALID before the resolver, all-zero\n            counters, no private rows or GETs, and unchanged input/runtime hashes.\n          - Run unique-target-member-order on fresh data with one reversed-order target and the\n            original four replies. Compare the complete guide-and-install acquisition, ordered\n            four-GET trace, literal safe/private reports, byte counts and cleanup.\n          - Record exact revision, command, report, traces, counters, resolver/effects audit,\n            before/after hashes and human result.\n        expected:\n          - \"Duplicate pair: invalid with exactly one INPUT_INVALID diagnostic at null\n            operation/issue/scope; issue/scope/private arrays empty, limits null, all\n            request/byte/elapsed counters zero, resolver_calls 0, server and client traces empty,\n            effects 0, cleanup_complete, Jira not_started and resolver settled. No secret access,\n            fallback or mutation.\"\n          - \"Unique reversed pair: complete with no diagnostics; 4/4/0 GETs in\n            issue→pointer→page→exact order; wire bytes 181+265+258+206=910, private serialized bytes\n            1154, resolver_calls 1, effects 0, cleanup_complete and unchanged input/runtime hashes.\n            The original literal guide acquisition is retained.\"\n          - Safe JSON omits private observations; no whole-domain discovery, receipt proof,\n            admission, human acceptance or activation is inferred from fixture completion.\n        evidence:\n          - Exact reviewed child revision and source import command, fixture and dependency identity.\n          - Safe report, private acquisition comparison, resolver and effects audit, GET trace, byte\n            counters, before/after input/runtime hashes and cleanup result.\n          - Retain any failed/unverified step with its actual stop point; local source observation\n            does not establish human, live-provider or installed acceptance.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain evidence and close disposable HTTPS fixture servers, sockets and timers; verify\n              cleanup_complete and unchanged input/runtime hashes.\n            - Remove only disposable fixture data. Preserve the reviewed source, original failure\n              record and retained reports. Make no live Jira or operational-state changes.\n  automated_regression: Two finite source subcases with literal zero-call rejection and four-call\n    positive-control oracles; retain the original packet and PGB-152 regressions, then run the\n    bounded affected source selection and both publication guards. Hosted CI and human acceptance\n    remain separate.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
