            "description": "R1-41 in the Pig Boss release-one set. This native-only catalog child makes the implemented source inspection and State repair records inspectable together. PGB-145 is its sole native completion prerequisite. Bind the exact reviewed runtime candidate and actual State/main ancestry before implementation; neither is bound by this publication. Human acceptance, PR checks, merge and activation remain separate.\n\n```yaml\n# Native title: Reconcile the source inspection delivery record\n# Source identity: provisional R1-41; actual native key assigned only by create/readback.\n# Reviewed plan SHA256: 64089b7feb21d36a4ed2fce8d2923c98d2475c6b27d433d92833dc1ee5ccd9e1\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: The implemented source inspection API and the offline repair preview have separate\n  reviewed delivery records. A contributor needs one truthful source catalog that preserves both\n  histories and shows the remaining source and native differences.\nprerequisites:\n  - ticket: PGB-145\n    required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    requirement: The catalog includes the implemented R1-36 contract and its four source human groups,\n      with 31 source Stories/136 groups and an explicit partial-inventory limitation.\n  - id: AC2\n    requirement: A reviewer can recover both complete prior publication records and all native\n      contracts, links, source/runtime fingerprints and dated observations without treating\n      historical counts as current.\n  - id: AC3\n    requirement: Current ownership, forecasts, dependencies and evidence distinguish source inspection,\n      catalog completion, installed PGB-147 work and final PGB-82 acceptance; no pending or accepted\n      human observation is reported PASS.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: codex/pgb150-source-inspection\n    change_boundary: One ten-path catalog PR stacked on the exact reviewed source runtime candidate;\n      compose the source delivery record and exact history guards only.\n    out_of_scope:\n      - No reader, fixture, source guide, installed Jira payload, provider probe, admission, policy,\n        proof, AWS, customer repository or PGB-144 decision change.\n      - No native inventory claim, new QA engine, generic history stripping, test oracle relaxation\n        or merge/activation authority.\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions: []\n  constraints:\n    - id: TAC1\n      requirement: Repository danielchappell/Pigboard; one ten-path PR stacked on the exact reviewed\n        runtime candidate. Its actual revision/tree and State/main ancestry must be bound in\n        implementation evidence before catalog coding; publication does not bind that future\n        candidate.\n    - id: TAC2\n      requirement: Preserve PGB-150 original 5 AC/4 TAC/4 human groups and 35 variants/eight\n        controls/private projection; retain PGB-152/PGB-154 repairs and all State runtime/history\n        records. Native PGB-145 is the catalog child’s only ai_qa_complete prerequisite; PGB-150\n        gains this child as an additional prerequisite.\n    - id: TAC3\n      requirement: Both whole predecessor publications and all nine complete amendment objects must\n        reconstruct exactly. Existing actual 25-file State runtime-byte checks remain live; missing,\n        changed, extra or reordered history fails instead of being stripped.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Exact reviewed source runtime candidate to be bound before implementation; actual\n      State/main a17841ee3e9e1a08a0ad3c322ae98fbff1cb41a9 and PGB-150 parent\n      7a06f7b25bbf79315f0a1e0763f1863d4b1f57f4 are planning context only, not the catalog\n      implementation base.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n    - id: DATA-01\n      description: Read-only source catalog, current native child/parent receipt, both predecessor\n        publication records, exact guard transcript and actual State runtime-byte comparison.\n      initial_state: Use the reviewed runtime plus catalog checkout with prepared dependencies and saved\n        read-only evidence. Do not access live Jira, change native records or synthesize a current\n        native inventory.\n      reference: null\n      preparation_id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n    - id: PREP-01\n      owner: implementer\n      supplies: PR-bound exact runtime/catalog revisions and trees, State/main ancestry, nine amendment\n        object hashes, two whole predecessor hashes, current native receipt, finite guard\n        command/result and 25-file runtime comparison.\n      used_by:\n        - DATA-01\n        - R1-41-H01\n      preserves:\n        - The original PGB-150 contract, four human groups and 35 variants/eight controls/private\n          projection.\n        - All PGB-152/PGB-154 and State history, links and dated counts; no new runtime test\n          campaign or current native inventory inferred.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: No approved automated QA skill executes this source-catalog comparison;\n      qa_skills are []. One designated human group remains NOT_RUN until separately observed or\n      dispositioned. Guard tests and independent code QA are separate evidence.\n    cases:\n      - id: R1-41-H01\n        execution: human\n        owner_role: designated human reviewer\n        requirements:\n          - AC1\n          - AC2\n          - AC3\n          - TAC1\n          - TAC2\n          - TAC3\n        prerequisites:\n          - PREP-01 supplies the exact reviewed runtime/catalog revisions, prepared dependencies,\n            complete native receipt and both predecessor publications.\n          - No credentials, live Jira, provider, Postman, UI or runtime fixture campaign is needed.\n        steps:\n          - Inspect the 31/136 source table, R1-36 contract, four human groups, 53 requirement rows\n            and 41 original scenarios. Compare the exact PGB-150 native body before and after the\n            catalog child prerequisite.\n          - Inspect the nine complete amendment hashes, both whole predecessor reconstructions,\n            current State/main ancestry, 8/10/18 file ownership and actual 25-file runtime-byte\n            comparison.\n          - Inspect the passing delivery guard transcript and compare current forecasts, pending\n            source/native differences, human NOT_RUN and CI/merge/activation statements with the\n            exact handoff evidence. Retain revision and comparison evidence.\n        expected:\n          - Every source entry and mapping agrees; current 31 Stories/136 groups is explicitly\n            partial. The original PGB-150 5 AC/4 TAC/4 human groups and existing prerequisites\n            remain unchanged except the actual catalog child prerequisite and concise ownership\n            note.\n          - Both complete predecessor publications reconstruct exactly; all nine amendment objects\n            and the actual 25-file runtime closure match their pinned hashes. Missing, changed,\n            extra or reordered history fails.\n          - Source runtime and catalog allocations are separate, installed PGB-147 and final PGB-82\n            acceptance remain pending, and no pending/accepted human observation is labelled PASS.\n            Any missing evidence remains unverified or NOT_RUN.\n        evidence:\n          - Exact reviewed runtime and catalog revisions/trees, current native receipt, before/after\n            parent body hashes and bound child key/link.\n          - 31/136/53/41 mapping, all nine object hashes, both predecessor hashes, 25-file runtime\n            comparison and guard transcript.\n          - Current forecasts, pending dependency/status notes and any failed or unverified check\n            with its stop point.\n        cleanup:\n          mode: prescribed\n          reason: null\n          owner: designated human reviewer\n          steps:\n            - Retain the comparison evidence and reviewed revisions; remove only disposable evidence\n              copies.\n            - Make no live Jira, provider, state, installation or activation change.\n  automated_regression: The two existing delivery-contract guard files assert exact current\n    composition, both predecessor restorations, all nine amendment objects and the actual State\n    runtime closure; run only their affected selection after implementation. Independent QA and\n    hosted checks remain separate.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
