            "description": "Director authorized this same-scope delivery allocation on 16 November 2026 after two independent full delivery-plan reviews. Exact-base planning, prerequisites, sizing and normal delivery gates remain required. No activation is authorized.\n\n```yaml\nschema: pigboard-ticket/v1\nproblem_to_solve: Manager history currently depends on old execution bodies and external observations that it no longer owns.\n  Its existing checker needs to distinguish exact historical authentication from proof that current work has recorded completion.\nprerequisites:\n- ticket: PGB-159\n  required_outcome: ai_qa_complete\nacceptance_criteria:\n- id: AC1\n  requirement: The existing handoff checker authenticates an exact historical target and required ancestry, including manager\n    admission and stack-update requests, without requiring a completed QA leaf.\n- id: AC2\n  requirement: Its separate completion purpose establishes recorded completion only for the exact current requirements, assignment\n    and complete leaf; changed or incomplete proof cannot pass.\n- id: AC3\n  requirement: Both results state that external freshness was not evaluated and grant no execution authority; no old work/context\n    reconstruction is required.\ntechnical_acceptance_criteria:\n  repository:\n    url: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard\n    base_branch: main\n    change_boundary: Validate authenticated recorded handoffs through the existing consumers and exact path forecast in the\n      delivery plan.\n    out_of_scope:\n    - Customer repository changes, activation or deployment\n    - Context service, public phase framework, parallel preview generation or new permission source\n    related_repositories: []\n  accepted_decisions:\n  - id: D-ROLE\n    decision: Owner10906 assigns Pig Boss complete deterministic scheduling and recorded-proof checks; workers retain current\n      applicable execution proof.\n    reference: https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-144?focusedCommentId=10906\n  - id: D-PREP\n    decision: Director10909 permits in-stage current fact preparation from existing authority; only the implementer fills\n      declared mechanical slots and every action requires its applicable proof.\n    reference: https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-144?focusedCommentId=10909\n  constraints:\n  - id: TAC1\n    requirement: Implement the planned inspectRecordedHistory and inspectRecordedCompletion contracts in the existing receipts\n      module and command, preserving strict public v1 record/chain behavior.\n  - id: TAC2\n    requirement: Retain authenticated actor/server metadata and original bytes, unique UUID/slot rules, current raw work/digest,\n      assignments, all repair roots, parent segments/cutoffs, retained tuples and genuine pre-first-PR inventory.\n  - id: TAC3\n    requirement: Use the closed manager envelope and canonical native authority specified in docs/delivery/manager-r1/role-amendment.md;\n      remove historical bodies/context and external PR/evidence inputs without manufacturing observations or replacing missing\n      retained proof with current comments.\ntesting_strategy:\n  testing_types: []\n  environment:\n    source: configured_target\n    target_reference: Current Pigboard PR checkout and prepared disposable local fixtures; no deployed customer target.\n    required_capabilities: []\n  actors: []\n  fixtures:\n  - id: DATA-01\n    description: Finite isolated fixtures for every control stated in this ticket; all other facts are valid and no earlier-priority\n      work exists.\n    initial_state: Fresh per control unless an ordered sequence is explicit; provider/model/helper outputs are simulated and\n      credentials dummy.\n    reference: null\n    preparation_id: PREP-01\n    owner: implementer\n  preparation:\n  - id: PREP-01\n    owner: implementer\n    supplies: Executable fixtures and exact source/copied commands or instruction invocations for the prescribed cases, bound\n      to the reviewed PR revision.\n    used_by:\n    - DATA-01\n    - PGB-160-H01\n    - PGB-160-H02\n    preserves:\n    - All prescribed inputs, ordering, expectations, evidence and cleanup; no invented authority, capability or live result.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI and instruction contracts that the approved API/database/UI helpers do not\n      execute; designated human reviewers run these cases. Developer regression and contributor QA evidence are separate.\n    cases:\n    - id: PGB-160-H01\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC1\n      - AC3\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Exact current QA completion, manager admission and stack-update targets with authenticated pages/retained tuples;\n        ordinary, repeated-parent/root and genuine pre-first-PR histories.\n      steps:\n      - Invoke history for each exact target and completion for the current completed leaf, without old work/context or external\n        observations.\n      - Change only hidden external PR head/target/open state; compare results and strict-v1 behavior on the reduced envelope.\n      expected:\n      - History validates the exact manager targets without claiming QA completion; completion proves only the valid current\n        completed leaf.\n      - Recorded results do not change merely because unseen external facts changed; external freshness remains unchecked\n        and strict v1 does not accept the reduced input as its old full proof.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n    - id: PGB-160-H02\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC2\n      - TAC2\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Isolated edited server metadata/body, conflicting UUID, changed current requirement, wrong assignment, missing ancestor/root,\n        conflicting QA slot, omitted first-PR inventory and missing parent-cutoff controls.\n      steps:\n      - Run each control for its relevant target/purpose using source and copied command.\n      - Inspect target, binding and diagnostic fields.\n      expected:\n      - Every missing, conflicting or mismatched proof fails its relevant purpose; no historical body or retained tuple is\n        synthesized and no result establishes completion from an unpublished or wrong target.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n  automated_regression: Update affected source/copied integration or instruction-contract regressions for these prescribed\n    outcomes, retain strict primitive/security regressions and run required repository checks.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
