the prescribed cases, bound\n      to the reviewed PR revision.\n    used_by:\n    - DATA-01\n    - PGB-161-H01\n    - PGB-161-H02\n    preserves:\n    - All prescribed inputs, ordering, expectations, evidence and cleanup; no invented authority, capability or live result.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI and instruction contracts that the approved API/database/UI helpers do not\n      execute; designated human reviewers run these cases. Developer regression and contributor QA evidence are separate.\n    cases:\n    - id: PGB-161-H01\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC1\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      prerequisites:\n      - Full current READY, review, QA and authorized human-rework inputs; authenticated old ancestry without old context;\n        actual own/required-parent PR, evidence and configured rights.\n      steps:\n      - Run each current purpose in source and copied checker.\n      - Repeat with changed PR identity/head/target, unsafe operation, missing prepared input, missing authority and mixed-version\n        controls.\n      expected:\n      - Valid current inputs pass only their explicit proof purpose without granting execution permission.\n      - Each current-proof failure rejects before its dependent action; prior recorded success cannot cure it and current\n        human rework retains current QA/same-open-PR proof.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n    - id: PGB-161-H02\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC2\n      - AC3\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Valid assignment with a declared future artifact unavailable; supported blocked/dependency-wait candidates and unknown\n        assignment/publisher or unsupported-kind controls.\n      steps:\n      - Validate assignment and unpublished candidate without fabricated native metadata.\n      - Validate real readback, then changed bytes/UUID and unknown-publication variants.\n      expected:\n      - Only an authorized supported inability shape validates; unknown assignment/rights or unsupported shapes remain local.\n      - Assignment success cannot replace full current readiness. Real readback binds the original candidate; changed/uncertain\n        publication fails or holds without replay, fake IDs or completion.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n  automated_regression: Update affected source/copied integration or instruction-contract regressions for these prescribed\n    outcomes, retain strict primitive/security regressions and run required repository checks.\nopen_questions: []\n```",
