rdering, expectations, evidence and cleanup; no invented authority, capability or live result.\n  dispatch_order: []\n  cases: []\n  human_review:\n    no_ai_cases_reason: Acceptance concerns CLI and instruction contracts that the approved API/database/UI helpers do not\n      execute; designated human reviewers run these cases. Developer regression and contributor QA evidence are separate.\n    cases:\n    - id: PGB-165-H01\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC1\n      - AC2\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      prerequisites:\n      - Prepared source/copied reviewer instruction harness with a current open PR, independent reviewer, current CI/approvals,\n        completed prepared inputs and authenticated old ancestry; clean and finding variants.\n      steps:\n      - Invoke the existing review route for each snapshot.\n      - Inspect current-proof checks, the one job invocation, all review categories and candidate/readback.\n      expected:\n      - Each snapshot receives one independent complete review with its prescribed clean/finding result.\n      - Old contexts are not reconstructed; current PR/CI/independence/prepared-input proof remains mandatory and no deployment\n        is invented for a static review.\n      evidence:\n      - Tested revision/pin, exact prepared commands or invocation, sanitized ordered action/result audit and observed outcome\n        for each named control; label simulated and actual evidence separately.\n      cleanup:\n        mode: prescribed\n        reason: null\n        owner: human QA reviewer\n        steps:\n        - Retain sanitized evidence, then remove only disposable local fixtures/build output; do not alter live records or\n          shared setup.\n    - id: PGB-165-H02\n      execution: human\n      owner_role: developer and human QA reviewer\n      requirements:\n      - AC3\n      - TAC1\n      - TAC2\n      - TAC3\n      prerequisites:\n      - Mis