      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"data\":{\"id\":\"10521\",\"key\":\"PGB-66\",\"fields\":{\"statuscategorychangedate\":\"2026-11-15T00:41:47.371+0100\",\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10053\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Epic\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"c9ff51a4-58ee-4c97-803f-6949e138918d\",\"hierarchyLevel\":1},\"components\":[],\"project\":{\"id\":\"10036\",\"key\":\"PGB\",\"name\":\"Pigboard Product\",\"projectTypeKey\":\"software\",\"simplified\":true},\"description\":\"## Current MVP tracking\\n\\nThis is the Pig Boss release-one MVP epic. The current implementation set contains **27 Stories**, after four reviewed same-scope splits: PGB-110 and PGB-132 from PGB-78, and PGB-113 and PGB-129 from PGB-81. The published Jira contracts contain 119 prescribed acceptance cases. These splits add no product features.\\n\\n* [All MVP Stories](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20PGB%20AND%20parent%20%3D%20PGB-66%20AND%20issuetype%20%3D%20Story%20ORDER%20BY%20key%20ASC)\\n* [Work in progress](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20PGB%20AND%20parent%20%3D%20PGB-66%20AND%20issuetype%20%3D%20Story%20AND%20status%20%3D%20%22In%20Progress%22%20ORDER%20BY%20key%20ASC)\\n* [Completed Stories](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20PGB%20AND%20parent%20%3D%20PGB-66%20AND%20issuetype%20%3D%20Story%20AND%20status%20%3D%20Done%20ORDER%20BY%20key%20ASC)\\n\\nUse the linked live lists for progress. Discovery and release-acceptance Tasks are separate from the 27-Story count. [PGB-114 — skill effectiveness evaluation](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-114) is a separate programme, outside this MVP.\\n\\nCount and navigation reconciled on 15 November 2026. The original approved baseline below is retained as history. The repository delivery records are being updated in the reviewed split PRs; Jira contains the current native Story set. Delivery automations remain inactive.\\n\\n## Pig Boss release one — approved implementation set\\n\\nPig Boss is Pigboard's deterministic manager. A company deploys it once into its AWS account for multiple projects in one Jira site. Workstream identity is Jira site + immutable project ID + full label: AI-Maria-1 in two projects represents two independent streams.\\n\\n## Approved release scope\\n\\n* One canonical configuration with project-specific mappings, permitted repositories and secret references.\\n* Portable scheduling policy and application logic, Jira adapter, DynamoDB scheduling state, thin Lambda wrapper and AWS deployment package.\\n* One scan at a time per installation; one responsible installation per project. Multiple independent Cursor streams can run concurrently.\\n* Ready to Work Story/Bug selection, queued repairs and stack updates, one occupied automated cycle per project-scoped stream and five Human Review tickets including Bugs.\\n* Existing stage webhooks launch workers; separate job/Jira skills produce typed evidence. Human-invoked request-rework remains separate from story writing.\\n* Customer-owned basic operating health: read-only readable/JSON inspection, completion freshness, failed/incomplete scans, budget warnings and AWS alarms with optional customer SNS routing.\\n* Install disabled, preview, readiness, safe stop/reconciliation, compatible upgrade/rollback/removal; no vendor runtime access.\\n\\n## Original approved implementation baseline\\n\\n23 Stories: PGB-71 through PGB-90 plus PGB-99 (company configuration), PGB-100 (health inspection), PGB-101 (AWS health alarms).          \\n104 prescribed acceptance cases; 53 product requirements; original 41 scheduling scenarios retained.          \\nEstimated effort: 35.25 human working days plus installed acceptance. Each Story is one Pigboard PR, at most 20 changed files and less than two days. Estimates are planning judgments.\\n\\n[Full ordered plan, sizing and cases](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/delivery/manager-r1/README.md).\\n[Company/health design](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md).\\n\\nThe revised design and delivery plan have two independent CLEAN reviews each. Native Story contracts were read back exactly after publication. The owner approved the complete 23-Story set on 15 November 2026 and authorized autonomous implementation, per-Story testing/review and merge after current-head CI and Codex bot approval. Execution follows the ordered delivery plan. Story status records progress; no AI execution labels are added. Delivery automations remain inactive.\\n\\n## Release acceptance\\n\\nPGB-91 verifies the installed package, including multi-project identity and health lifecycle; PGB-58 verifies actual worker delivery; PGB-92 records the later activation decision. Local checks and historical provider probes do not prove installed acceptance. A second disposable Jira project and any test notification destination need explicit access before that installed test; no resources are created by grooming.\\n\\n## Follow-on work\\n\\nPGB-94 is the high-priority path to measured 50-project capacity. Ten is a benchmark step, not a supported-project limit. Measure the workload, optimize safe reads, and only then design partitioning if needed; preserve one installation/configuration and one writer per project.\\n\\nPGB-95: automatic Jira/Cursor provisioning. PGB-70: worker status visibility. PGB-63 → PGB-64 → PGB-65: launch/cancel feasibility, dispatch design and grooming. PGB-62: human unblock and blocked-stage display. PGB-98: Teams blocker alerts. PGB-60: separate PR environment pipeline. PGB-96: additional QA helpers. PGB-97: other customer-cloud packages.\\n\\nNo worker heartbeat/transcript collection, Cursor deduplication, dispatcher, automatic recovery, SaaS or old runtime reuse in this release. Basic Pig Boss health is explicitly included.\\n\\n## History and evidence\\n\\nPGB-67/68 discovery and PGB-69 baseline grooming remain completed historical records. The isolated provider proof is PARTIAL, not release acceptance. PGB-93 records this approved company/health delta. Prior merged design/review evidence is preserved in PRs 73 and 74; this description supersedes older label-global and all-monitoring-deferred wording. Implementation and merge are now authorized for this fixed set; activation remains a separate owner gate.\",\"fixVersions\":[],\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":4,\"key\":\"indeterminate\",\"colorName\":\"yellow\",\"name\":\"In Progress\"},\"timetracking\":{},\"attachment\":[],\"workratio\":-1,\"summary\":\"Coordinate company work with Pig Boss\",\"issuerestriction\":{\"issuerestrictions\":{},\"shouldDisplay\":true},\"watches\":{\"watchCount\":1,\"isWatching\":true},\"lastViewed\":\"2026-11-15T23:54:36.181+0100\",\"creator\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"subtasks\":[],\"created\":\"2026-11-14T14:20:45.720+0100\",\"reporter\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"aggregateprogress\":{\"progress\":0,\"total\":0},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"labels\":[\"owner-approved\",\"pgb-manager-r1\",\"scope-frozen\"],\"versions\":[],\"progress\":{\"progress\":0,\"total\":0},\"issuelinks\":[{\"id\":\"10617\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10003\",\"name\":\"Relates\",\"inward\":\"relates to\",\"outward\":\"relates to\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10362\",\"key\":\"PGB-58\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Current MVP: configure Jira and Cursor delivery\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"High\",\"id\":\"2\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10618\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10003\",\"name\":\"Relates\",\"inward\":\"relates to\",\"outward\":\"relates to\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10525\",\"key\":\"PGB-70\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Investigate worker status visibility after the first manager release\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10619\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10003\",\"name\":\"Relates\",\"inward\":\"relates to\",\"outward\":\"relates to\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10519\",\"key\":\"PGB-64\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Review the scope and design for reliable agent dispatch\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10665\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10000\",\"name\":\"Blocks\",\"inward\":\"is blocked by\",\"outward\":\"blocks\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10554\",\"key\":\"PGB-94\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Measure and plan Pig Boss capacity for 50 projects\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"High\",\"id\":\"2\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10666\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10000\",\"name\":\"Blocks\",\"inward\":\"is blocked by\",\"outward\":\"blocks\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10555\",\"key\":\"PGB-95\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Design Jira and Cursor setup from one configuration\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10667\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10000\",\"name\":\"Blocks\",\"inward\":\"is blocked by\",\"outward\":\"blocks\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10556\",\"key\":\"PGB-96\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Plan additional prescribed QA capabilities\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10668\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10000\",\"name\":\"Blocks\",\"inward\":\"is blocked by\",\"outward\":\"blocks\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10557\",\"key\":\"PGB-97\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Plan a second customer-owned deployment package\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}},{\"id\":\"10669\",\"type\":{\"id\":\"10000\",\"name\":\"Blocks\",\"inward\":\"is blocked by\",\"outward\":\"blocks\"},\"outwardIssue\":{\"id\":\"10558\",\"key\":\"PGB-98\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Define customer Teams alerts for blocked work\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"To Do\",\"id\":\"10048\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":2,\"key\":\"new\",\"colorName\":\"blue-gray\",\"name\":\"To Do\"}},\"priority\":{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"id\":\"3\"},\"issuetype\":{\"id\":\"10056\",\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"Task\",\"subtask\":false,\"entityId\":\"6c8818f3-60c0-4276-9ef8-e0df65804083\",\"hierarchyLevel\":0}}}}],\"votes\":{\"votes\":0,\"hasVoted\":false},\"comment\":{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"10355\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Reviewed design and ratified target diagrams are published for merge in https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/64 (head e63dedd685548731caa74b222c3ac1ea2b321e5b). Scope: customer-owned AWS Lambda admission; monitoring/duplicate prevention remain follow-on work. Design: docs/architecture/manager-release-one.md; ordered queue: docs/architecture/manager-release-one-plan.md; review evidence: docs/architecture/review-record.md. Two independent design reviews and two fresh plan reviews returned CLEAN for Task grooming only; two further reviewers passed all 17 committed documentation files. CI and current-revision Codex bot thumbs-up are still required before merge. PGB-67 and PGB-68 block PGB-69. This record does not mark any discovery or implementation complete and authorizes no live deployment or activation.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-14T14:25:56.086+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-14T14:25:56.086+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10359\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Publication verified: PR64 merged as 79548bda36794b78d99b49c388c162059298c2ff. Codex review https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/64#issuecomment-6877949260 completed with no findings on exact head e63dedd685548731caa74b222c3ac1ea2b321e5b; bot +1 observed before merge. Both hosted CI runs passed. Post-merge file tree equals reviewed head. All nine ratified target diagrams are now linked from the README. PGB-66/67/68/69/70 remain To Do, with no execution labels; PGB-67 and PGB-68 block PGB-69. No runtime or delivery automation was activated.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-14T14:30:08.129+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-14T14:30:08.129+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10362\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Owner clarified the launch QA contract: use current skills, keep all prescribed cases on the ticket, explicitly pair AI cases with their skills, and keep a separate human testing section pending for Human Review. Unsupported AI-assigned execution still blocks; no silent reassignment or new database skill in this release. PGB-67 records this. DynamoDB state/lifecycle discovery continues; stack-cascade authority remains an open decision and no implementation Story is ready.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-14T15:26:09.140+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-14T15:26:09.140+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10365\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Published and merged interim discovery update: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/65. Merge revision 89356976870bec7bcfb7f14aa812c60d5c32af0a; reviewed head b57bab872173ab7796ccead5ae73a6127c165c5b. Two independent design reviews and two fresh committed-publication reviews CLEAN, local checks passed, both hosted checks passed, and Codex completed current-head review with no findings and its own thumbs-up (https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/65#issuecomment-6878841669). Merged file tree matches reviewed head.\\n\\nState/upgrade contract: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/architecture/manager-state.md  \\nDiscovery/AI-human QA ownership: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/architecture/manager-discovery.md\\n\\nThis is publication of approved direction and explicit open design gates, not completion of PGB-67/PGB-68. Automatic stack cascading remains a proposal; exact admission/reconciliation safety and full contract/fixture evidence remain unfinished. PGB-69 stays dependent on discovery; complete fixed implementation Stories still require owner review. No runtime, skill execution, AWS provisioning or delivery automation activation occurred.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-14T15:36:48.736+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-14T15:36:48.736+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10369\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"## Approved stack-repair rule — 14 November 2026\\n\\nThe owner approved conservative stack repair using the actual recorded parent PR/revision, not Epic order or an AI impact assessment. Each ticket retains its own PR.\\n\\nWhen publishing B, its implementer records B's PR, parent A's PR, parent revision incorporated and B's revision covered by verification. A confirmed repair to A uses A's existing ticket and PR. An active B finishes its existing automated cycle first; do not interrupt it or start C ahead of queued repair.\\n\\nAfter A's repair completes automated review and prescribed AI QA and reaches Human Review at a new revision, the manager compares B's recorded parent revision. If B still requires the recorded stack update, the manager owns Human Review -> Rework Queued, with the repair link and reason. Then normal admission moves B -> In Progress. B incorporates A's repaired code on B's branch and gets fresh review/AI QA, preserving pending human tests. Continue actual descendants oldest first; matching already-incorporated repair evidence must prevent repeated queuing.\\n\\nMissing/ambiguous relationships, already-merged PRs or scope growth require human intervention. Routine merge/retarget activity and an independent B do not trigger cascading. No multi-PR bug repair job, PR merge/retarget automation, interruption or additional QA skill support is authorized.\\n\\nThis resolves cascade policy and manager queue authority. Exact handoff schema, transition safeguards, repeat-repair behavior, five-ticket cap accounting and fixture proof remain discovery work. No live automation or ticket execution is enabled.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-14T15:51:34.404+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-14T15:51:34.404+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10412\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"The complete first-manager MVP implementation set is ready for owner review, not execution. Product/design PR #73 is merged; the reviewed delivery pack is PR #74: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/74\\n\\nBoth independent Sol delivery-plan reviews are CLEAN: 20/20 Stories, 88/88 prescribed cases, 50/50 requirements, 41/41 scenarios, with a second sweep. A native Bug eligibility gap was fixed in implementer/reviewer/QA ownership and installed acceptance before final review.\\n\\nAll 20 structured YAML bodies were read back and parsed from Jira, matching the reviewed contracts after prerequisite-key substitution. 45/45 directed dependency links were verified. All Stories remain To Do with owner-review-required and no AI label.\\n\\n| Story | Outcome | Prerequisites | Human-day estimate |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| PGB-71 | Validate an editable work document | Reviewed design | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-72 | Check the complete prescribed test plan | PGB-71 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-73 | Write complete Epic and ticket YAML | PGB-71, PGB-72 | 1.25 |\\n| PGB-74 | Validate assignment and handoff evidence | PGB-71, PGB-72 | 1.75 |\\n| PGB-75 | Hand an implemented PR to review | PGB-73, PGB-74 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-76 | Review and hand off the current PR | PGB-74, PGB-75 | 1.25 |\\n| PGB-77 | Execute prescribed QA helper steps | PGB-72, PGB-74 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-78 | Complete QA with an honest evidence ledger | PGB-74, PGB-76, PGB-77 | 1.75 |\\n| PGB-79 | Request rework through the human’s assistant | PGB-74 | 1.25 |\\n| PGB-80 | Preview ready work from a complete snapshot | PGB-72, PGB-74 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-81 | Preview the complete repair order | PGB-80 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-82 | Preview current Jira work with bounded reads | PGB-81 | 1.75 |\\n| PGB-83 | Install a disabled AWS preview | PGB-82 | 1.75 |\\n| PGB-84 | Inspect durable scheduling state | PGB-83 | 1.75 |\\n| PGB-85 | Reconcile an uncertain attempt with evidence | PGB-82, PGB-84 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-86 | Upgrade and remove the AWS installation safely | PGB-84, PGB-85 | 1.25 |\\n| PGB-87 | Admit a ready Story or Bug safely | PGB-75, PGB-76, PGB-78, PGB-82, PGB-84, PGB-85, PGB-86 | 1.75 |\\n| PGB-88 | Admit queued rework on its existing PR | PGB-79, PGB-87 | 1.25 |\\n| PGB-89 | Queue a completed dependent PR for repair | PGB-88 | 1.5 |\\n| PGB-90 | Check a compatible release before enabling delivery | PGB-73, PGB-75, PGB-76, PGB-77, PGB-78, PGB-79, PGB-89 | 1.5 |\\n\\nTotal forecast 30.25 human working days, including tests/docs/PR prep, plus installed acceptance; this is estimated effort, not calendar or AI-token cost. Every Story is one Pigboard PR, under two days and at most 20 files (schema move deletions included). Detailed file forecasts and all cases are in the review pack.\\n\\nOperational gates: PGB-91 installed manager acceptance; existing PGB-58 actual worker acceptance (including native Story and Bug); PGB-92 later owner activation decision. Existing provider proof stays PARTIAL; previously unrun checks are explicit future acceptance, not retroactively passed.\\n\\nPGB-67/68 discovery is complete. PGB-69 grooming now awaits final publication checks and owner review. No manager implementation, AWS deployment, worker test or automation activation occurred. Monitoring, duplicate launch prevention, cancellation, new QA engines, human-unblock production and environment provisioning remain follow-on work.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-14T22:37:38.186+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-14T22:37:38.186+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10425\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Design and grooming completed in [PR #75](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/75), merged as `65b9d8efe9ad0b729756e62c7cf0f07a0ea25c1d`. The merged tree exactly matches independently reviewed head `6631b98f44eea06176ca3a647d61e67a1e910078`; both review lenses are CLEAN, both current-head CI checks passed, and the Codex review bot completed with no findings and a thumbs-up.\\n\\nPig Boss now has the agreed project-scoped workstream identity, one installation/multiple projects, basic health inspection and AWS alarms in the proposed release. The complete owner-review set has 23 Stories, 104 prescribed cases, 53 mapped requirements and 54 dependency links. All 104 cases have explicit implementer preparation bindings. Eight corrected Jira bodies were read back exactly; statuses and worker labels remain unchanged.\\n\\nThe three added Stories are PGB-99 (company configuration), PGB-100 (operating health) and PGB-101 (health alarms). PGB-94 is the high-priority plan to measure and reach 50-project capacity; 10 is a benchmark step, not a cap. Deferred work is linked in the [roadmap](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/product/follow-on-roadmap.md).\\n\\n[Complete ordered Story set](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/delivery/manager-r1/README.md) · [Design](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md).\\n\\nThis closes design/grooming only. The 23 Stories remain To Do and require final owner review before implementation. No manager runtime, installed acceptance, delivery run or automation activation was performed.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T00:34:04.906+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T00:34:04.906+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10426\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Owner approved the complete 23-Story set on 15 November 2026 and authorized autonomous implementation, per-Story PRs and merges through the entire Epic. Fixed scope remains the PR75 design/plan at main `65b9d8efe9ad0b729756e62c7cf0f07a0ea25c1d`. Astra authors each detailed plan; Sol implements, independently reviews and performs QA. Each Story requires meaningful verification, independent gates, current-head CI and Codex bot thumbs-up before merge. Returned findings take priority over starting/continuing new work. Out-of-scope findings become separate owner-mentioned Jira work outside this Epic. Delivery automations remain inactive; installed acceptance and activation are distinct from code merge.\\n\\nStarting PGB-71. Jira remains the active queue; each Story will carry exact plan, tests, review and merge evidence. Approved ordered set: PGB-71,72,73,74,99,75,76,77,78,79,80,81,82,83,84,85,86,100,101,87,88,89,90.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T00:41:45.586+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T00:41:45.586+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10427\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Owner QA execution clarification, 15 November 2026: existing QA skills may assume Safeguard/AWS or be unsuitable/token-wasteful. If a concrete skill problem occurs, preserve evidence, file a separate post-epic bug and mention the owner, stop using the affected skill, and continue direct developer/independent QA against the Story requirements. Keep all required test coverage and truthful outcomes. Skill bugs will be reviewed after this Epic; this does not expand its frozen scope. No skill defect is asserted merely because a skill is not needed.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T00:50:45.955+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T00:50:45.955+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10549\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Delivery checkpoint — 15 November 2026: 5/23 approved implementation Stories are merged and verified: PGB-71/PR77, PGB-72/PR78, PGB-73/PR79, PGB-74/PR80 and PGB-99/PR81. A separately tracked prerequisite regression, PGB-102/PR82, is also merged after both independent code reviews, source/installed QA, current-head CI and Codex bot thumbs-up. Main is `3d9f135cd8cb412269b8eaa4a7245ba7b419a115`; its tree was verified against the reviewed head.\\n\\nPGB-75 is the active Story. Its corrected candidate `a6635c43dc632eb20c15f09c829de2cb454133a2` has both independent whole-change code reviews CLEAN, 253 passing repository tests and passing branch CI. Six bounded actual-agent QA exercises are in progress; original failed QA remains preserved. No PGB-75 PR/merge or final QA pass is claimed yet. PGB-76 remains provisional planning only; remaining Stories retain the approved order. All delivery automations remain inactive. Formal human/live acceptance and activation gates stay separate from implementation completion. No added product scope.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T07:27:53.031+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T07:27:53.031+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10570\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"# Pig Boss parallel delivery addendum — revision 1, 15 November 2026\\n\\nStatus: proposed reorder of the already approved fixed 23 Stories; ready for two independent Sol reviews together with the separate PGB-80 implementation plan. No requirement, dependency, acceptance, activation or merge gate is removed. This is delivery coordination, not a product redesign or a new Story.\\n\\nEvidence: live `/private/tmp/pgb66-live-children-20261115.json` contains all 29 Epic children, including exactly 23 Stories. Six Stories are Done (71–75 and 99); 17 remain. Current source baseline is verified merged main `9f03c1561b0e32de05cd296b24e50885f4abbe91`. Jira owns current status; this dated plan is not a second status store. Forecasts below are the approved `docs/delivery/manager-r1/plan-metadata.json` estimates, not new readiness claims. Every later Story still needs an actual current-tree implementation plan.\\n\\n## Two workstreams and the integration join\\n\\nA owns delivery skills: 76 → 77 → 78, then 79 (79 is dependency-ready now but its shared skill/manifest surfaces make this deliberate sequencing useful). B owns the manager: 80 → 81 → 82 → 83 → 84 → 85 → 86. These two chains may implement concurrently, in separate branches/worktrees. B's health 100 becomes dependency-ready after 84; 101 requires 86 and 100. After the principal chains join, integration 87 → 88 → 89 → 90 is serial. Health 100/101 can occupy the second implementation lane alongside integration 87–89 when per-Story shared-file ownership permits. This is not a claim that all 17 are independent.\\n\\nThe currently dependency-eligible Stories are 76, 77, 79 and 80. Start the already reviewed 76 and, only after its own plan gate, 80. Do not start four implementations just because four prerequisites are satisfied. 77's provisional plan is preserved; it does not compete with active 76 edits.\\n\\n| Story | Workstream / outcome | Exact prerequisite Stories | Approved forecast days / paths | Current readiness |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| PGB-76 | A: reviewer handoff | 74,75 | 1.25 / 8 | In Progress; actual reviewed plan supersedes forecast: 1.55 / 20 |\\n| PGB-77 | A: prescribed QA helpers | 72,74 | 1.5 / 7 | To Do; provisional actual plan 1.75 / 18, not yet reviewed |\\n| PGB-78 | A: complete QA ledger | 74,76,77 | 1.75 / 10 | Wait for 76 and 77 |\\n| PGB-79 | A: human request-rework | 74 | 1.25 / 7 | Dependency-ready; sequence behind A's active work |\\n| PGB-80 | B: offline complete-snapshot preview | 72,74,99 | 1.75 / 7 | Dependency-ready; concrete plan accompanies this addendum |\\n| PGB-81 | B: repair-order preview | 80 | 1.5 / 7 | Wait for 80 |\\n| PGB-82 | B: bounded Jira reads | 81,99 | 1.75 / 12 | Wait for 81 |\\n| PGB-83 | B: disabled AWS preview installation | 82 | 1.75 / 13 | Wait for 82 |\\n| PGB-84 | B: durable state inspection | 83 | 1.75 / 10 | Wait for 83 |\\n| PGB-85 | B: evidence-only reconciliation | 82,84 | 1.5 / 7 | Wait for 84 |\\n| PGB-86 | B: upgrade and removal | 84,85 | 1.25 / 8 | Wait for 85 |\\n| PGB-100 | B/health: operating health | 83,84,99 | 1.75 / 11 | Eligible after 84; can run alongside integration when files permit |\\n| PGB-101 | B/health: health alarms | 86,100 | 1.5 / 10 | Wait for both; required by final release check |\\n| PGB-87 | Integration: ordinary admission | 75,76,78,82,84,85,86 | 1.75 / 10 | Explicit skills/manager join; no early apply implementation |\\n| PGB-88 | Integration: queued repair admission | 79,87 | 1.25 / 5 | Requires human request skill as well as apply |\\n| PGB-89 | Integration: dependent stack queue | 88 | 1.5 / 5 | Serial with 88 on apply code |\\n| PGB-90 | Integration: compatible release check | 73,75,76,77,78,79,89,101 | 1.5 / 15 | Final join; PGB-58 live delivery acceptance remains a separate referenced gate |\\n\\n## Ownership and merge sequencing\\n\\n* Root maintains one active Jira queue, exact revisions, dependencies and gate evidence. Astra authors plans only. Sol implements; different Sol agents review and independently execute QA.\\n* A uses `/private/tmp/pigboard-product-requirements-20261114` and owns its current skill/composer/Jira-reference/automation changes. B uses `/private/tmp/pigboard-manager-stream-20261115`, initially `codex/pgb-80-manager-preview`, and owns manager policy, preview CLI and the approved config additions. Nobody edits another agent's working tree or reverts unrelated changes.\\n* Shared sources are explicit: README, ARCHITECTURE, docs/install, docs/using-pigboard, docs/workflow, config/skill-bundle, distribution/install tests, and later canonical configuration, Lambda/template and lifecycle files. A/B may each have distinct additive changes in isolated branches; neither overwrites the other's whole file. Root chooses a merge order. The second branch rebases onto verified merged main, preserves both changes, reruns affected contract/distribution tests and obtains review for any conflict resolution or new behavior. Identical reviewed file-tree preservation may be recorded as such; new changes never inherit a stale CLEAN verdict.\\n* PGB-80 specifically shares README, ARCHITECTURE, manifest, install guide/installer/test with 76. Its manager/config runtime is disjoint. Final installed manifest must include both reviewer migration and preview payload, with both smoke/contract checks. Sequence publication/merge, not source ownership, through root. Do not merge either branch's historical main over the other's completed work.\\n* After 84, health touches Lambda/config and later AWS template/lifecycle. Root allocates those files exclusively per active phase. Prefer 85/86 first, then health alongside 87–89; serialize any simultaneous Lambda/template/install-guide edits, or prepare them in isolated branches with explicit reviewed integration. No shared dirty checkout. If dependencies or a safe file partition are unavailable, the second slot does review/QA/preparation instead of inventing work.\\n* A newly returned CI/bot/code/QA finding on a prerequisite takes priority over next-Story work in its lane and any dependent integration. Save a checkpoint, fix confirmed in-scope root causes, re-review current revision and rebind dependants after merge. Independent unaffected work in the other lane may continue. Shared contract defects pause both affected consumers. Out-of-scope defects are recorded without expanding the frozen Story.\\n\\n## Capacity and gates\\n\\nThere are four active-agent slots including root. Maximum two active implementations leaves root + one QA/review slot. A two-reviewer round needs root + two independent reviewers, so pause one implementation/planner at a saved checkpoint; pause both if an independent QA run also needs the slot. Reviewers may run sequentially if necessary, but remain two distinct independent Sol authors with complementary lenses. Do not substitute an implementer's self-review. A plan author may not independently approve its own plan.\\n\\nEach Story retains: actual Jira/current-source plan → two CLEAN plan reviews → implementation and meaningful tests/docs → committed exact-diff two CLEAN code reviews + independent QA → PR/current CI/current Codex completed thumbs-up → authorized merge → resulting tree verification. Plan previews are marked provisional. Local tests do not complete prescribed human acceptance or activate a customer installation. At most 20 changed source paths and less than two human working days apply independently to each complete Story, including supporting docs/tests/PR work; split before code if a genuine limit cannot be met.\\n\\nThe present bounded review round covers **two separately hashed artifacts**: this 17-Story reorder and PGB-80's concrete plan. Each reviewer enumerates 17/17 rows, the dependency joins/ownership/capacity/gates, and separately all PGB-80 requirements/contracts/paths, with second-sweep coverage and a verdict per artifact. Approval of the reorder is not approval of all future implementation plans.\\n\\nExisting QA helper defects use the owner's explicit fallback: preserve concrete failed evidence, file a post-Epic bug, stop the unsuitable helper and use direct independent QA. The missing advertised qa-database npm test file is such a pre-existing tooling defect; it does not cancel PGB-77 or authorize unbounded test infrastructure repair.\\n\\n## Seven-principle assessment\\n\\n1. Intuitive: two named delivery lanes and one explicit final join replace a misleading globally serial queue; users still see ordinary Jira Stories and outcomes.\\n2. Discoverable: every remaining Story lists prerequisites, forecast and readiness. Agents receive exact working directories/file ownership and reviewers receive finite denominators.\\n3. Delightful: independent work proceeds while the other lane waits for gates, without repeated approval questions or crowding out QA. Capacity limits may briefly idle one lane; this avoids costly conflicted work.\\n4. Token saver: reuse ratified designs and saved provisional plans; exchange exact revisions and bounded deltas. Never conceal failed evidence or skip review to reduce calls.\\n5. Secure: separate checkouts and explicit authority prevent accidental writes/reverts; provider/state/activation boundaries are unchanged. Parallel delivery grants no broader product privileges.\\n6. Agents are equal: explicit machine-readable Jira dependencies and exact artifact hashes accompany human-readable queue explanations. Both lanes receive the same independent gates.\\n7. Dependable: dependency-ready, planned, implemented, tested, reviewed, merged and accepted remain different states. Returned findings stop affected dependants; no stale review result or pending PR is called merged.\\n\\nOne canonical customer configuration remains the product authority. Parallel ownership changes implementation order only; no duplicated settings, runtime state, scheduler, monitoring, deduplication or activation is introduced.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T08:41:14.512+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T08:41:14.512+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10573\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Parallel delivery addendum SHA256 `ffe8be4cd55ee2c65a0068d28cfa1154c4cf7dc742344b6a36bfe6048e908382` has two independent Sol CLEAN reviews: 17/17 remaining Story rows, 43/43 dependency edges, ownership/merge/4-slot capacity and all seven principles. Full reports are recorded on PGB-80. The owner authorized two concurrent streams: skills (76–79) and manager (80–86,100–101), then actual dependency joins 87–90. No new scope, removed review gate or activation; all automations remain inactive. PGB-80's distinct implementation plan is still in corrective review; approval of this delivery reorder does not approve unreviewed Story plans.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T08:41:16.749+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T08:41:16.749+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10609\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Owner reaffirmed the frozen-scope boundary during delivery: plan/code reviewers assess the agreed Stories and cannot add requirements or expand scope. Reject proposed additions. Worthwhile out-of-scope problems are separate follow-on tickets at the end of the backlog, outside this frozen Epic; optional work must not delay current delivery. Confirmed defects against existing acceptance criteria still receive scoped fixes and verification; no unmet approved criterion is silently called complete. Current delivery: PGB76 merged/Done (7/23 implementation Stories complete); PGB77 started after two clean bound-plan reviews; PGB80 PR85 has a bounded installation-guide correction plus already-approved parallel-branch integration underway. All delivery automations remain inactive.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T09:54:30.349+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T09:54:30.349+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10662\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Delivery ownership update, authorized by the owner on 15 November:\\n\\n* Foundation manager owns PGB-80–86 in dependency order.\\n* Skills/Admission manager owns PGB-77–78, then PGB-87–90 when their prerequisites are merged.\\n* Health manager will start PGB-100 after PGB-84; PGB-101 also waits for PGB-86.\\n* Director owns cross-stream dependencies, conflict coordination, final current-revision gates, serialized PR merges and verification of main. Managers own branch changes, feedback fixes, tests and independent reviews. No concurrent independent merges.\\n\\nPGB-77 has merged in [PR #90](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/90), merge `4e561839f5588a97c34a960dcfb7e21964fb9d1a`. Its merged tree exactly matches the reviewed/tested tree. This brings merged implementation Stories to 9/23. Human acceptance, deployment and activation remain separate; delivery automations stay inactive.\\n\\nThis is contributor coordination only. The fixed product scope, dependencies and review gates are unchanged.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T12:09:16.324+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T12:09:16.324+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10679\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Director-authorized same-scope PGB-81 split (15 November 2026): [PGB-80](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-80) → [PGB-113](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-113) / R1-25 (existing repeated-parent chain validation, C01–C03) → [PGB-81](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-81) / R1-11 (complete offline repair preview, unchanged four AC, two TAC and all 42 cases) → [PGB-82](https://scubapig.atlassian.net/browse/PGB-82). Existing PGB-80→81 and every other dependency remain.\\n\\nReviewed structural packet: `/private/tmp/pgb81-core-split-proposal-r4.md`, SHA256 `ff10a7531a5bdd7c5e3455479d013dc01d6a2a39d036e2c4f707cd14409d687f`; independent product/technical structural CLEAN reports: `/private/tmp/pgb81-director-split-product-r4.md` (`65d096102fe0b5b09e6bd27810427c4135ffdebbfb4ca0d18708e66e641b6c8d`) and `/private/tmp/pgb81-director-split-technical-r4.md` (`955f45617a3dd75cbf381b5330a116b47ac4b60220302e508a402958523edf2e`). Publication/readback evidence is retained at `/private/tmp/pgb81-split-publication-20261115`.\\n\\nForecast: validator 15 paths/1.85 human days including both source record updates and native publication; final preview 19 paths/1.70 days. This adds one Story and three cases to the current delivery set; PGB-110/R1-24 and PGB-78 remain independently owned. Source publication is pending the first validator PR and must bind the actual merged PGB-110 records without changing their bodies, cases, order or evidence. Historical 23-Story/104-case publication remains historical.\\n\\nProvisional — not ready for delivery: corrected/verified PGB-80 merge, current-base binding and two fresh concrete-plan reviews remain required before coding. All new and original human acceptance cases remain NOT_RUN. No implementation, merge, release, provider test or automation activation is established by this publication.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T13:49:17.590+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T13:49:17.590+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10694\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Owner delivery-process decision — Astra owns repair planning (15 November 2026).\\n\\nWhen a test failure, QA finding, review finding, integration problem or implementation obstacle requires a changed plan, Sol stops the affected implementation and preserves the evidence. Sol may reproduce the issue and gather bounded diagnostics; it must not improvise successive repairs outside the approved plan.\\n\\nAn Astra planning agent diagnoses the actual root cause against the requirements and current revision, classifies the finding, and writes a concrete repair plan or amendment. The plan identifies affected files, behavior, meaningful verification, documentation/integration effects and remaining size. Both existing independent complementary Sol plan reviews must be CLEAN before Sol resumes the repair. Normal exact-commit QA/code reviews, hosted CI and current-head Codex approval remain required.\\n\\nUnchanged authorized work may continue. Mechanical steps already explicitly covered by the approved plan do not require restarting planning, but a new diagnosis, changed algorithm, expected-result correction or unplanned repair approach returns to Astra. Preserve original failures and independently assess input/oracle corrections; do not weaken tests to obtain a pass.\\n\\nScope and sizing rules are unchanged: no reviewer-driven scope growth; track out-of-scope work separately; autonomously split coherent same-scope oversized Stories. Current managers must check their in-flight corrections for uncovered deviations without discarding valid completed work. This is the contributor operating process, not an expansion of the Pigboard MVP, customer-worker configuration or frozen evaluation treatments.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-15T16:02:22.769+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-15T16:02:22.769+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"10925\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"body\":\"Published the reviewed role-delivery allocation under the Director's integration disposition.\\n\\n* PGB-159: complete scheduling declarations; PGB-160: authenticated recorded handoffs; PGB-161: current worker proof and truthful inability; PGB-162: recorded-proof offline preview; PGB-163: exact native handoffs and reconciliation history.\\n* PGB-164, PGB-165 and PGB-166: existing implementer, reviewer, and QA/human-rework caller changes. PGB-167 is the separate five-file documentation Task.\\n* PGB-82 retains its identity, parent, To Do status, original five AC/three TAC/four cases, with only the reviewed additions and dependencies on PGB-162/163. PGB-144 remains completed.\\n\\nAll nine Story contracts (including residual PGB-82) were read back against the reviewed draft after mechanical real-key binding. Sixteen new Blocks links were verified; no private issue aliases or null prerequisite keys remain. Current Epic inventory at this readback is 50 Stories and 7 Tasks (57 children); this is native inventory, not a shipped/source-catalogue count.\\n\\nBoth independent full delivery-plan reviews are CLEAN for plan SHA256 `98916b2ab8dab5e36fc2f753c97b94e2f0e49fe3f188e8a09dbacdc00f397aa4`, covering all nine contracts, 59 criteria, 22 designated human case groups and 76 distinct planned paths. No acceptance execution is claimed. Product review SHA256 `ccb42f76c8cf0f7bd053986fd64e17496cffcbddad36488e859fba62ccec8370`; technical review SHA256 `13fa2c0a9552f57689a9839cca7eeaf5415749150d21ebd40db7cdb3f7f91d9a`.\\n\\nPGB-81 finishes naturally. PGB-159 follows its actual completed base and must recheck its tight 20-file/12–15.5h whole-slice forecast before code. The first later Core change owns the complete machine catalogue/guard amendment; PGB-167 contains no such code. The 84.5–117h mapped Core/caller subtotal excludes later host/State/apply/release work and is neither net amendment cost nor total remaining project cost. Later source-dependent sizing remains provisional. Normal planning, code review, checks, Director merge and separate acceptance gates remain; automations stay inactive.\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"712020:61741bca-1777-4e2c-bf07-d25f03103b7d\",\"emailAddress\":\"daniel@scubapig.software\",\"displayName\":\"Joseph Chappell\",\"active\":true,\"timeZone\":\"Europe/Madrid\",\"accountType\":\"atlassian\"},\"created\":\"2026-11-16T12:40:34.600+0100\",\"updated\":\"2026-11-16T12:40:34.600+0100\",\"jsdPublic\":true}],\"maxResults\":17,\"total\":17,\"startAt\":0},\"assignee\":null,\"worklog\":{\"startAt\":0,\"maxResults\":20,\"total\":0,\"worklogs\":[]},\"updated\":\"2026-11-16T12:40:34.600+0100\",\"status\":{\"description\":\"\",\"name\":\"In Progress\",\"id\":\"10049\",\"statusCategory\":{\"id\":4,\"key\":\"indeterminate\",\"colorName\":\"yellow\",\"name\":\"In Progress\"}},\"customFields\":{\"Development\":{\"id\":\"customfield_10000\",\"value\":\"{}\"},\"Rank\":{\"id\":\"customfield_10019\",\"value\":\"0|i002lw:\"}}},\"appliedContentFormat\":\"markdown\"}}"
