                  "body": "The complete first-manager MVP implementation set is ready for owner review, not execution. Product/design PR #73 is merged; the reviewed delivery pack is PR #74: https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/74\n\nBoth independent Sol delivery-plan reviews are CLEAN: 20/20 Stories, 88/88 prescribed cases, 50/50 requirements, 41/41 scenarios, with a second sweep. A native Bug eligibility gap was fixed in implementer/reviewer/QA ownership and installed acceptance before final review.\n\nAll 20 structured YAML bodies were read back and parsed from Jira, matching the reviewed contracts after prerequisite-key substitution. 45/45 directed dependency links were verified. All Stories remain To Do with owner-review-required and no AI label.\n\n| Story | Outcome | Prerequisites | Human-day estimate |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PGB-71 | Validate an editable work document | Reviewed design | 1.5 |\n| PGB-72 | Check the complete prescribed test plan | PGB-71 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-73 | Write complete Epic and ticket YAML | PGB-71, PGB-72 | 1.25 |\n| PGB-74 | Validate assignment and handoff evidence | PGB-71, PGB-72 | 1.75 |\n| PGB-75 | Hand an implemented PR to review | PGB-73, PGB-74 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-76 | Review and hand off the current PR | PGB-74, PGB-75 | 1.25 |\n| PGB-77 | Execute prescribed QA helper steps | PGB-72, PGB-74 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-78 | Complete QA with an honest evidence ledger | PGB-74, PGB-76, PGB-77 | 1.75 |\n| PGB-79 | Request rework through the human’s assistant | PGB-74 | 1.25 |\n| PGB-80 | Preview ready work from a complete snapshot | PGB-72, PGB-74 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-81 | Preview the complete repair order | PGB-80 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-82 | Preview current Jira work with bounded reads | PGB-81 | 1.75 |\n| PGB-83 | Install a disabled AWS preview | PGB-82 | 1.75 |\n| PGB-84 | Inspect durable scheduling state | PGB-83 | 1.75 |\n| PGB-85 | Reconcile an uncertain attempt with evidence | PGB-82, PGB-84 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-86 | Upgrade and remove the AWS installation safely | PGB-84, PGB-85 | 1.25 |\n| PGB-87 | Admit a ready Story or Bug safely | PGB-75, PGB-76, PGB-78, PGB-82, PGB-84, PGB-85, PGB-86 | 1.75 |\n| PGB-88 | Admit queued rework on its existing PR | PGB-79, PGB-87 | 1.25 |\n| PGB-89 | Queue a completed dependent PR for repair | PGB-88 | 1.5 |\n| PGB-90 | Check a compatible release before enabling delivery | PGB-73, PGB-75, PGB-76, PGB-77, PGB-78, PGB-79, PGB-89 | 1.5 |\n\nTotal forecast 30.25 human working days, including tests/docs/PR prep, plus installed acceptance; this is estimated effort, not calendar or AI-token cost. Every Story is one Pigboard PR, under two days and at most 20 files (schema move deletions included). Detailed file forecasts and all cases are in the review pack.\n\nOperational gates: PGB-91 installed manager acceptance; existing PGB-58 actual worker acceptance (including native Story and Bug); PGB-92 later owner activation decision. Existing provider proof stays PARTIAL; previously unrun checks are explicit future acceptance, not retroactively passed.\n\nPGB-67/68 discovery is complete. PGB-69 grooming now awaits final publication checks and owner review. No manager implementation, AWS deployment, worker test or automation activation occurred. Monitoring, duplicate launch prevention, cancellation, new QA engines, human-unblock production and environment provisioning remain follow-on work.",
