                  "body": "Design and grooming completed in [PR #75](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/pull/75), merged as `65b9d8efe9ad0b729756e62c7cf0f07a0ea25c1d`. The merged tree exactly matches independently reviewed head `6631b98f44eea06176ca3a647d61e67a1e910078`; both review lenses are CLEAN, both current-head CI checks passed, and the Codex review bot completed with no findings and a thumbs-up.\n\nPig Boss now has the agreed project-scoped workstream identity, one installation/multiple projects, basic health inspection and AWS alarms in the proposed release. The complete owner-review set has 23 Stories, 104 prescribed cases, 53 mapped requirements and 54 dependency links. All 104 cases have explicit implementer preparation bindings. Eight corrected Jira bodies were read back exactly; statuses and worker labels remain unchanged.\n\nThe three added Stories are PGB-99 (company configuration), PGB-100 (operating health) and PGB-101 (health alarms). PGB-94 is the high-priority plan to measure and reach 50-project capacity; 10 is a benchmark step, not a cap. Deferred work is linked in the [roadmap](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/product/follow-on-roadmap.md).\n\n[Complete ordered Story set](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/delivery/manager-r1/README.md) · [Design](https://github.com/danielchappell/Pigboard/blob/main/docs/architecture/pig-boss-operations.md).\n\nThis closes design/grooming only. The 23 Stories remain To Do and require final owner review before implementation. No manager runtime, installed acceptance, delivery run or automation activation was performed.",
